1
00:00:17,718 --> 00:00:20,548
(Tongyeong, South Gyeongsang Province)

2
00:00:30,758 --> 00:00:34,968
(A lush, green spring in May)

3
00:00:35,668 --> 00:00:37,498
Yes, that's really cute.

4
00:00:37,498 --> 00:00:38,938
(A pier in a fishing village)

5
00:00:39,638 --> 00:00:42,268
(Yum Jung Ah, Roh Yoon Seo)

6
00:00:43,378 --> 00:00:44,408
Wait.

7
00:00:44,408 --> 00:00:46,548
(Kang You Seok, Kim Sun Young)

8
00:00:50,148 --> 00:00:52,248
- You Seok looks so cute.
- Yes!

9
00:00:52,248 --> 00:00:53,648
(Laughing)

10
00:00:54,298 --> 00:00:55,868
(Giggling)

11
00:00:55,874 --> 00:00:57,744
(Surprised)

12
00:00:58,259 --> 00:00:59,289
- What?
- Are you leaving?

13
00:00:59,289 --> 00:01:01,789
- What's going on? Hold on.
- Why?

14
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:03,459
What's going on here?

15
00:01:03,459 --> 00:01:04,599
- What's happening?
- What?

16
00:01:04,999 --> 00:01:06,099
What's this?

17
00:01:06,829 --> 00:01:07,929
What's going on?

18
00:01:07,929 --> 00:01:09,199
- Hey.
- Wait a minute.

19
00:01:09,329 --> 00:01:10,339
- Wait...
- This can't be true.

20
00:01:10,339 --> 00:01:11,339
- Seriously?
- Wait.

21
00:01:11,339 --> 00:01:12,339
What are they doing?

22
00:01:12,339 --> 00:01:13,339
Wait a minute.

23
00:01:13,909 --> 00:01:15,109
- I'm hungry.
- No!

24
00:01:15,309 --> 00:01:16,739
- Goodness.
- What do you do about them?

25
00:01:17,439 --> 00:01:18,679
What are you doing?

26
00:01:18,679 --> 00:01:20,249
Where are you going?

27
00:01:20,249 --> 00:01:22,109
Gosh, they're so cruel.

28
00:01:22,449 --> 00:01:23,479
Jung Ah.

29
00:01:23,479 --> 00:01:24,849
(Fresh off the Sea 3)

30
00:01:24,849 --> 00:01:27,349
I don't even see them anymore.

31
00:01:27,849 --> 00:01:30,889
(A month ago)

32
00:01:30,889 --> 00:01:32,859
I'm nervous.

33
00:01:32,889 --> 00:01:34,089
- Really?
- Yes.

34
00:01:34,859 --> 00:01:36,929
This feeling of starting something new.

35
00:01:38,059 --> 00:01:39,199
Hey, Kim Sun Young.

36
00:01:40,229 --> 00:01:41,899
Hello.

37
00:01:42,629 --> 00:01:44,069
- Jung Ah.
- Yes?

38
00:01:44,499 --> 00:01:45,799
You look pretty today.

39
00:01:47,309 --> 00:01:48,569
I just came from home.

40
00:01:48,569 --> 00:01:49,639
Don't lie to me.

41
00:01:49,639 --> 00:01:51,609
I've been to your place, and you weren't dressed like that.

42
00:01:51,739 --> 00:01:53,709
What are you talking about?

43
00:01:53,709 --> 00:01:54,979
You're unbelievable.

44
00:01:54,979 --> 00:01:56,919
My goodness.

45
00:01:57,049 --> 00:01:58,379
- It hasn't been that long.
- Didn't you come...

46
00:01:58,379 --> 00:01:59,419
to my house two months ago?

47
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:01,689
- It's only been 2 months?
- Was it less than 2 months ago?

48
00:02:02,419 --> 00:02:04,859
(Meanwhile, someone arrives.)

49
00:02:05,189 --> 00:02:06,989
You Seok, we were just talking about you.

50
00:02:07,289 --> 00:02:09,129
- Should I come back later?
- Hello.

51
00:02:09,229 --> 00:02:10,999
- No, come in.
- No.

52
00:02:11,099 --> 00:02:13,229
- Hello.
- We know each other, right?

53
00:02:13,229 --> 00:02:14,499
- Right.
- Really?

54
00:02:14,569 --> 00:02:16,399
- We just...
- We met each other a while ago.

55
00:02:16,399 --> 00:02:18,539
- We worked on something together.
- We met each other...

56
00:02:18,539 --> 00:02:19,539
about four hours ago.

57
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:22,209
We'll be filming together two weeks later.

58
00:02:22,269 --> 00:02:23,979
Hello, it's nice to meet you.

59
00:02:24,179 --> 00:02:25,539
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you too.

60
00:02:25,539 --> 00:02:27,209
- You've never met each other?
- No, it's our first time.

61
00:02:27,449 --> 00:02:28,779
- We've never met before.
- Right.

62
00:02:28,779 --> 00:02:29,949
I've seen her a lot...

63
00:02:29,949 --> 00:02:31,379
- on TV.
- On TV?

64
00:02:32,149 --> 00:02:34,389
(She finds him adorable.)

65
00:02:34,389 --> 00:02:35,719
Do you know Yoon Seo?

66
00:02:35,719 --> 00:02:38,259
- She and I were in a drama before.
- I see.

67
00:02:38,259 --> 00:02:40,229
Then we all know each other.

68
00:02:40,229 --> 00:02:41,729
I haven't worked face-to-face...

69
00:02:41,859 --> 00:02:43,259
- with Yoon Seo, - Didn't you work together once?

70
00:02:43,259 --> 00:02:44,459
but we were in a drama together.

71
00:02:45,199 --> 00:02:46,399
(The youngest...)

72
00:02:46,399 --> 00:02:47,729
(who's met everyone here has arrived.)

73
00:02:47,729 --> 00:02:49,969
- Hello.
- Our youngest is here.

74
00:02:49,969 --> 00:02:51,699
- What is it?
- What's that?

75
00:02:51,869 --> 00:02:53,439
- Hello.
- Come in.

76
00:02:53,439 --> 00:02:54,469
My goodness.

77
00:02:54,469 --> 00:02:56,239
- It's been a long time.
- Yoon Seo, what did you bring?

78
00:02:56,239 --> 00:02:57,309
She brought a present.

79
00:02:57,539 --> 00:02:59,139
- Look at her.
- Hello.

80
00:02:59,709 --> 00:03:02,209
- I haven't seen you in a long time.
- Have you been well?

81
00:03:02,209 --> 00:03:03,379
Long time, no see.

82
00:03:03,379 --> 00:03:05,249
- Hasn't it been years?
- Yes.

83
00:03:05,449 --> 00:03:06,889
- Have you been well?
- It's good to see you.

84
00:03:07,189 --> 00:03:08,949
We were so close before.

85
00:03:08,949 --> 00:03:10,519
(The youngest who's attached to her)

86
00:03:11,159 --> 00:03:12,419
What's all this?

87
00:03:12,419 --> 00:03:14,529
Wait, let me explain.

88
00:03:14,589 --> 00:03:16,299
Yesterday was Arbor Day.

89
00:03:16,299 --> 00:03:18,599
- You're right.
- I've gotten into plants lately.

90
00:03:18,599 --> 00:03:20,229
- Really?
- I picked out one...

91
00:03:20,229 --> 00:03:22,029
that would suit each of you.

92
00:03:22,069 --> 00:03:23,699
One that suits each person?

93
00:03:23,699 --> 00:03:24,699
Based on the vibe?

94
00:03:24,699 --> 00:03:26,539
I don't know if you keep plants,

95
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:28,909
but having one at home makes me feel good.

96
00:03:28,909 --> 00:03:31,679
- Yoon Seo, you have a kind heart.
- Thank you.

97
00:03:31,679 --> 00:03:32,739
My goodness.

98
00:03:32,979 --> 00:03:35,209
I've only seen Yoon Seo 2 or 3 times...

99
00:03:35,209 --> 00:03:36,649
- at movie premieres.
- During the "Smugglers" premiere.

100
00:03:36,649 --> 00:03:38,549
Right, during the "Smugglers" premiere,

101
00:03:38,549 --> 00:03:40,719
I went to say hello.

102
00:03:40,719 --> 00:03:42,019
- Right.
- She came running all the way...

103
00:03:42,019 --> 00:03:43,759
from a distance just to say hello.

104
00:03:43,759 --> 00:03:45,819
- I heard that.
- We never worked together before.

105
00:03:45,819 --> 00:03:46,889
Right.

106
00:03:46,889 --> 00:03:49,089
- Jung Ah told me about that.
- She hugged me like this.

107
00:03:49,929 --> 00:03:52,999
Every time I watched her on screen, I thought she was so beautiful.

108
00:03:53,099 --> 00:03:55,999
When she came over to say hello, she was even prettier.

109
00:03:56,399 --> 00:03:57,569
Thank you.

110
00:03:57,569 --> 00:03:59,269
(Embarrassed by the compliment)

111
00:03:59,269 --> 00:04:01,869
- This is great.
- Everyone knows each other.

112
00:04:01,869 --> 00:04:03,209
We've met at least once.

113
00:04:03,309 --> 00:04:05,039
I have so many questions to ask.

114
00:04:05,039 --> 00:04:06,409
(Even though I know a lot about you, I have a lot to ask.)

115
00:04:06,649 --> 00:04:09,619
Where's your hometown? What's your family like?

116
00:04:09,619 --> 00:04:10,679
- Jung Ah.
- Yes?

117
00:04:11,049 --> 00:04:12,149
- Okay.
- Yes.

118
00:04:12,149 --> 00:04:13,719
- Can I...
- Really?

119
00:04:13,719 --> 00:04:15,749
- Can I talk about myself?
- Sure.

120
00:04:15,749 --> 00:04:17,059
I like talking about myself.

121
00:04:17,059 --> 00:04:18,089
You start, You Seok.

122
00:04:18,089 --> 00:04:19,089
About me...

123
00:04:19,389 --> 00:04:21,589
My hometown is Gangneung in Gangwon Province.

124
00:04:22,229 --> 00:04:25,359
I lived there until I was 19.

125
00:04:25,359 --> 00:04:27,429
My grandfather was a farmer...

126
00:04:27,669 --> 00:04:28,669
- when I was a kid.
- My gosh.

127
00:04:28,669 --> 00:04:29,669
What did he grow?

128
00:04:30,069 --> 00:04:34,909
- He mostly grew potatoes and rice.
- In Gangwon Province?

129
00:04:34,909 --> 00:04:37,409
Those were his main crops.

130
00:04:37,409 --> 00:04:38,409
- Rice?
- Then...

131
00:04:38,409 --> 00:04:41,009
- Rice and potatoes?
- I've never had to buy rice.

132
00:04:42,919 --> 00:04:43,919
That's real privilege.

133
00:04:43,919 --> 00:04:45,779
Then you must be good at working in the fields and rice paddies.

134
00:04:45,779 --> 00:04:47,489
Not really.

135
00:04:47,489 --> 00:04:49,719
When I go help out, I'm just the snack assistant.

136
00:04:49,719 --> 00:04:50,889
I bring them snacks.

137
00:04:50,889 --> 00:04:51,889
(Far from working in the field)

138
00:04:51,889 --> 00:04:53,659
- So you don't know how to farm?
- I'm clumsy.

139
00:04:53,659 --> 00:04:55,259
- You have no farming skills?
- I have no farming skills.

140
00:04:55,259 --> 00:04:57,159
Originally, I studied art.

141
00:04:58,159 --> 00:05:00,129
I went to an arts high school.

142
00:05:00,129 --> 00:05:02,499
- Sunhwa Arts School?
- How do you know?

143
00:05:02,499 --> 00:05:03,639
I looked everything up.

144
00:05:03,639 --> 00:05:05,369
Is that when you started studying art?

145
00:05:05,369 --> 00:05:08,169
I also majored in fine arts in college.

146
00:05:08,469 --> 00:05:09,709
- At Ewha Womans University, right?
- Yes.

147
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:10,909
You studied western painting.

148
00:05:10,909 --> 00:05:13,249
Yes, I luckily got in.

149
00:05:13,249 --> 00:05:14,279
That's great.

150
00:05:14,509 --> 00:05:15,949
Yoon Seo is also famous...

151
00:05:15,949 --> 00:05:17,819
for having a good fashion sense.

152
00:05:17,819 --> 00:05:19,279
- No way.
- Really?

153
00:05:19,279 --> 00:05:21,449
- Isn't it a bit overwhelming?
- How do you know so much about her?

154
00:05:22,089 --> 00:05:24,559
(She's Yoon Seo's unofficial spokesperson.)

155
00:05:24,889 --> 00:05:26,119
A lot of information came up.

156
00:05:26,119 --> 00:05:27,389
- Maybe because I searched a lot.
- Really?

157
00:05:28,059 --> 00:05:30,099
I heard that you really wanted to be on this show.

158
00:05:30,099 --> 00:05:31,229
- Me?
- Yes.

159
00:05:31,229 --> 00:05:33,299
Even though you were incredibly busy,

160
00:05:33,699 --> 00:05:36,199
you wanted to make time for it.

161
00:05:36,199 --> 00:05:37,539
- I did.
- To experience country life?

162
00:05:37,539 --> 00:05:39,299
- What was the reason?
- It was...

163
00:05:39,299 --> 00:05:41,009
watching Fresh Off the Sea 1 and 2.

164
00:05:41,869 --> 00:05:43,579
I've been a huge fan of Jung Ah since I was young.

165
00:05:44,009 --> 00:05:45,279
- I wanted to work with her.
- I should treat him...

166
00:05:45,279 --> 00:05:46,409
- exceptionally well.
- I've admired her.

167
00:05:46,409 --> 00:05:48,949
The moment I heard you were on it, I said yes without hesitation.

168
00:05:48,949 --> 00:05:49,949
- Me too.
- But...

169
00:05:49,949 --> 00:05:51,619
I also enjoyed watching Fresh off the Sea 1 and 2.

170
00:05:51,949 --> 00:05:53,349
Seriously.

171
00:05:53,349 --> 00:05:55,349
It was a show I've wanted to be a part of.

172
00:05:55,749 --> 00:05:57,989
It was very healing.

173
00:05:57,989 --> 00:05:59,059
(That's how people who truly love Fresh off the Sea...)

174
00:05:59,059 --> 00:06:00,129
(and Jung Ah came together.)

175
00:06:00,259 --> 00:06:03,499
I watched the entire season over 2 or 3 days until 4am.

176
00:06:03,499 --> 00:06:05,159
I even paused it when I went to the bathroom.

177
00:06:05,659 --> 00:06:08,129
I don't know why it was so important to watch you do every single thing,

178
00:06:08,129 --> 00:06:09,739
but I still wanted to pause it.

179
00:06:09,739 --> 00:06:12,169
I paused it, went to the bathroom, and put it back on.

180
00:06:12,499 --> 00:06:14,139
I watched the whole thing in an hour.

181
00:06:14,669 --> 00:06:16,339
It was that impactful in my life.

182
00:06:17,039 --> 00:06:18,379
I made up my mind this time.

183
00:06:19,009 --> 00:06:20,149
I'm going to live for the viewers.

184
00:06:20,279 --> 00:06:21,349
(Is that so?)

185
00:06:21,349 --> 00:06:23,119
You gave me so much comfort...

186
00:06:23,119 --> 00:06:24,849
that I want to pass on that feeling.

187
00:06:24,849 --> 00:06:26,279
- The comfort you received?
- Exactly.

188
00:06:26,949 --> 00:06:29,859
- And I'll do my best.
- Yes, that's a good idea.

189
00:06:30,289 --> 00:06:33,029
I'm curious to see how you guys are going to live together.

190
00:06:33,329 --> 00:06:35,529
I'm the complete opposite of you.

191
00:06:35,529 --> 00:06:36,599
(I sleep in and like to lie around.)

192
00:06:36,599 --> 00:06:38,929
- All three of you? That's harsh.
- At least I am.

193
00:06:38,929 --> 00:06:40,099
I'm the opposite of you.

194
00:06:40,099 --> 00:06:42,369
- Why don't you ever take a break?
- Right.

195
00:06:42,369 --> 00:06:44,869
- When you rest, I can rest too.
- I heard that you didn't rest.

196
00:06:45,269 --> 00:06:47,169
- I'm not the type to lie around.
- I know.

197
00:06:47,639 --> 00:06:49,139
You say, "Let's get some rest."

198
00:06:49,139 --> 00:06:50,609
Then three seconds later, you're back on your feet.

199
00:06:50,609 --> 00:06:53,109
- Then we have to get up with her.
- Right.

200
00:06:53,109 --> 00:06:54,749
Are you all spontaneous types?

201
00:06:54,749 --> 00:06:56,009
- You don't like spontaneous people?
- Are you a spontaneous type too?

202
00:06:56,209 --> 00:06:57,219
(Smiling)

203
00:06:57,219 --> 00:06:59,179
- Are you a spontaneous type?
- That's wonderful.

204
00:06:59,179 --> 00:07:00,249
All of them are spontaneous.

205
00:07:00,249 --> 00:07:01,789
I'm the type who follows planners really well.

206
00:07:01,789 --> 00:07:04,289
- Me too.
- We love planners.

207
00:07:04,289 --> 00:07:05,989
I'll be the only one making all the plans.

208
00:07:05,989 --> 00:07:07,959
(Jung A realizes that road ahead won't be easy.)

209
00:07:07,959 --> 00:07:10,029
Who's going to make the bed? The three of us will sleep together.

210
00:07:10,029 --> 00:07:11,599
- I make the bed.
- I'll do it.

211
00:07:12,129 --> 00:07:13,669
- Really?
- Yes.

212
00:07:13,669 --> 00:07:15,669
I've never made my bed in my life.

213
00:07:15,669 --> 00:07:16,739
Not once.

214
00:07:17,869 --> 00:07:18,899
- What?
- Yes.

215
00:07:19,199 --> 00:07:20,839
Seriously, I've never made my bed.

216
00:07:20,839 --> 00:07:22,539
Have you? You'd better be honest.

217
00:07:22,539 --> 00:07:23,579
Sometimes.

218
00:07:23,579 --> 00:07:24,709
I can't say never.

219
00:07:24,709 --> 00:07:26,449
- You make your bed when you get up?
- No,

220
00:07:26,449 --> 00:07:28,449
- I rarely do it.
- See?

221
00:07:28,449 --> 00:07:30,719
But I do it sometimes.

222
00:07:30,719 --> 00:07:32,279
- What does this mean?
- When someone comes to visit...

223
00:07:32,279 --> 00:07:33,619
You make your bed because...

224
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:35,519
- Exactly.
- someone is coming to your house.

225
00:07:35,519 --> 00:07:36,689
But after sleeping...

226
00:07:36,689 --> 00:07:37,859
This is going to be rough.

227
00:07:37,859 --> 00:07:38,859
(She's getting shocked several times today.)

228
00:07:38,859 --> 00:07:41,259
- But I'm quite obedient.
- Really?

229
00:07:41,559 --> 00:07:43,499
Don't you prefer people who quietly follow along?

230
00:07:43,499 --> 00:07:44,499
- Right.
- Instead of those who lead...

231
00:07:44,499 --> 00:07:45,659
Without talking back?

232
00:07:45,659 --> 00:07:46,999
- Without talking back?
- Without talking back?

233
00:07:46,999 --> 00:07:48,229
I might talk back sometimes.

234
00:07:48,229 --> 00:07:50,099
(Switching into playful mode)

235
00:07:50,839 --> 00:07:52,199
I got it, you rascal.

236
00:07:52,199 --> 00:07:53,209
(He's got some nerve.)

237
00:07:53,209 --> 00:07:54,709
I don't think You Seok will be easy to handle.

238
00:07:55,339 --> 00:07:56,679
- Right.
- He doesn't listen.

239
00:07:57,809 --> 00:07:59,979
(The mischievous one loves getting attention from the older ladies.)

240
00:08:00,349 --> 00:08:03,149
- You watched Fresh off the Sea.
- Yes.

241
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,849
From watching it, what did you want to try the most?

242
00:08:04,849 --> 00:08:06,319
Playing games...

243
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,119
and making bets with the production crew.

244
00:08:08,589 --> 00:08:09,619
What are you good at?

245
00:08:09,619 --> 00:08:10,859
- What are you good at?
- I'm very curious.

246
00:08:10,859 --> 00:08:12,389
- Are you strong?
- No, I'm not very strong.

247
00:08:12,389 --> 00:08:13,659
I'm clever.

248
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:15,989
- You're smart?
- What kind of smart?

249
00:08:16,359 --> 00:08:17,599
- Are you good with petty tricks?
- Exactly.

250
00:08:17,599 --> 00:08:18,799
You're good at coming up with petty tricks?

251
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:20,499
That's great. You must be good at games.

252
00:08:20,499 --> 00:08:21,629
Yes, I'm good at games.

253
00:08:21,629 --> 00:08:23,939
- You're good at playing games?
- Yes.

254
00:08:23,939 --> 00:08:24,939
When deciding who does the dishes,

255
00:08:24,939 --> 00:08:26,169
- We should play a game.
- we should play a game.

256
00:08:26,469 --> 00:08:28,109
We could make some money,

257
00:08:28,109 --> 00:08:30,209
bet with...

258
00:08:30,209 --> 00:08:31,439
- the production crew.
- Bet with them again?

259
00:08:31,439 --> 00:08:33,009
- Then we can multiply the amount.
- Again?

260
00:08:33,009 --> 00:08:34,379
- He's only thinking about games.
- We can multiply it.

261
00:08:34,609 --> 00:08:35,949
Yes, that's a good idea.

262
00:08:36,109 --> 00:08:37,779
We must come up with games that we can win.

263
00:08:38,149 --> 00:08:39,179
Those that work in our favor?

264
00:08:39,319 --> 00:08:40,849
- Yes.
- But they don't go the way we want.

265
00:08:41,289 --> 00:08:44,759
What I'd like to do is earn money,

266
00:08:45,059 --> 00:08:47,059
- buy ingredients, and cook.
- Make food?

267
00:08:47,059 --> 00:08:48,259
I'd like to cook.

268
00:08:48,259 --> 00:08:50,499
I'd like to cook for Jung Ah.

269
00:08:50,499 --> 00:08:52,759
(Showing attention toward Jung Ah)

270
00:08:52,759 --> 00:08:54,229
I'd like to cook for Jung Ah.

271
00:08:54,229 --> 00:08:56,669
(She's the first person who wants to cook for Jung Ah.)

272
00:08:56,669 --> 00:08:58,099
- She's such a good daughter.
- She really is.

273
00:08:58,099 --> 00:08:59,839
It's because you end up cooking every time.

274
00:09:00,139 --> 00:09:02,409
Jung Ah, why don't you take a break this time?

275
00:09:02,409 --> 00:09:05,339
You're saying that because you haven't been out there yet.

276
00:09:06,039 --> 00:09:07,249
- That's true.
- It's not that kind of situation.

277
00:09:07,249 --> 00:09:08,649
All of us are dreaming now.

278
00:09:08,649 --> 00:09:11,149
There's no time to relax and fool around.

279
00:09:11,149 --> 00:09:12,149
I understand, Jung Ah.

280
00:09:12,149 --> 00:09:13,489
- It's a war.
- It must be a battlefield.

281
00:09:13,489 --> 00:09:16,989
Why? It was so comforting to watch.

282
00:09:16,989 --> 00:09:17,989
(It's a war!)

283
00:09:17,989 --> 00:09:20,489
(What will shake up the siblings)

284
00:09:20,489 --> 00:09:21,889
- Why isn't it working?
- I can't lift it.

285
00:09:22,159 --> 00:09:25,199
(A new battleground)

286
00:09:25,859 --> 00:09:29,999
(Nature that refuses to compromise)

287
00:09:30,399 --> 00:09:33,969
(A scale that has grown relentlessly bigger)

288
00:09:34,469 --> 00:09:36,609
(Tougher than ever)

289
00:09:38,139 --> 00:09:41,449
(More intense than ever)

290
00:09:42,709 --> 00:09:43,749
(This time,)

291
00:09:43,749 --> 00:09:44,979
(Fresh off the Sea will become...)

292
00:09:44,979 --> 00:09:46,989
(something unlike before.)

293
00:09:48,119 --> 00:09:51,619
(One month later)

294
00:09:51,659 --> 00:09:54,629
(Tongyeong)

295
00:09:57,499 --> 00:09:58,759
We have to start the engine.

296
00:09:58,829 --> 00:10:00,669
I will try it for now.

297
00:10:00,669 --> 00:10:01,999
(The production crew seems unusually busy today.)

298
00:10:02,769 --> 00:10:05,239
(It feels like something is about to happen today.)

299
00:10:05,869 --> 00:10:07,609
(Without a single suspicions,)

300
00:10:07,609 --> 00:10:09,869
(a car pulls in.)

301
00:10:10,279 --> 00:10:13,509
Hello, I look forward to working with you.

302
00:10:13,509 --> 00:10:14,709
(Second Eldest Sun Young arrives first.)

303
00:10:15,049 --> 00:10:16,719
I woke up so early...

304
00:10:17,779 --> 00:10:18,849
because my heart was fluttering.

305
00:10:20,389 --> 00:10:22,889
(While Sun Young is feeling nervous)

306
00:10:24,419 --> 00:10:25,659
Hello.

307
00:10:25,659 --> 00:10:27,989
(The siblings' 3rd eldest, You Seok arrives 2nd.)

308
00:10:28,289 --> 00:10:29,929
- Gosh, look at him.
- This is great.

309
00:10:29,929 --> 00:10:31,659
(Making his entrance with confidence)

310
00:10:31,659 --> 00:10:33,099
Are you the first one to arrive?

311
00:10:33,429 --> 00:10:35,399
You should've arrived first.

312
00:10:36,299 --> 00:10:37,799
- There was some traffic.
- You Soon.

313
00:10:37,799 --> 00:10:38,899
Yes.

314
00:10:38,899 --> 00:10:40,469
- I told you to call me by my name.
- Yes, Sun Young.

315
00:10:40,609 --> 00:10:41,609
Okay.

316
00:10:41,609 --> 00:10:43,609
The viewers may not fully understand the situation yet.

317
00:10:44,709 --> 00:10:46,649
The two of you, how do you feel?

318
00:10:46,809 --> 00:10:48,749
I feel great. The weather is beautiful.

319
00:10:48,749 --> 00:10:50,079
I don't know how long this will last, but...

320
00:10:50,079 --> 00:10:51,119
I don't feel that great.

321
00:10:52,119 --> 00:10:54,249
- Why?
- I feel the pressure...

322
00:10:54,249 --> 00:10:55,419
to make the viewers happy.

323
00:10:55,949 --> 00:10:58,859
(Sun Young only knows the viewers and nothing else.)

324
00:10:58,859 --> 00:11:00,359
I'm determined to work hard...

325
00:11:00,359 --> 00:11:01,989
for the next three days for the viewers.

326
00:11:02,689 --> 00:11:03,729
I feel pressured.

327
00:11:04,529 --> 00:11:06,129
(Youngest Yoon Seo arrives.)

328
00:11:06,129 --> 00:11:07,229
Hello.

329
00:11:08,299 --> 00:11:11,069
(She hugs Sun Young as soon as she arrives.)

330
00:11:11,839 --> 00:11:15,469
Jung Ah. What did I tell you?

331
00:11:15,469 --> 00:11:16,469
(Captain Yum is the last to arrive.)

332
00:11:16,469 --> 00:11:17,909
You said that you'd dress up.

333
00:11:18,409 --> 00:11:19,439
Do I look bad?

334
00:11:19,709 --> 00:11:21,479
I didn't know what to do with my hair.

335
00:11:21,579 --> 00:11:24,519
- Jung Ah.
- I did what I could... Hello.

336
00:11:24,519 --> 00:11:25,579
Your hair looks nice today.

337
00:11:25,649 --> 00:11:27,719
- My hair...
- You put it towards the front.

338
00:11:27,719 --> 00:11:28,889
I didn't dry it completely.

339
00:11:28,889 --> 00:11:30,859
- I don't know how to style it.
- It looks great right now.

340
00:11:30,859 --> 00:11:33,859
We'll start with the poster shoot on the boat...

341
00:11:33,859 --> 00:11:35,159
because the weather is nice.

342
00:11:35,389 --> 00:11:38,259
(A poster photo shoot is scheduled on a boat today.)

343
00:11:38,559 --> 00:11:39,759
Where should we go?

344
00:11:39,999 --> 00:11:41,729
- Do we go in right away?
- Yes.

345
00:11:41,729 --> 00:11:44,499
There must be a room assigned...

346
00:11:44,499 --> 00:11:46,139
to each of us.

347
00:11:46,139 --> 00:11:47,369
This is fascinating.

348
00:11:47,539 --> 00:11:49,709
There's no name on it. Do we go in wherever we want?

349
00:11:51,679 --> 00:11:54,079
(On the yellow, orange, red, and green bungalows)

350
00:11:54,549 --> 00:11:58,049
(Instead of their names, cue cards are attached.)

351
00:11:58,649 --> 00:12:00,549
Pick the color you want.

352
00:12:03,119 --> 00:12:04,259
"Fresh off the Sea."

353
00:12:04,259 --> 00:12:09,059
(The siblings pick a bungalow without the slightest suspicion.)

354
00:12:09,989 --> 00:12:11,229
(Click)

355
00:12:13,929 --> 00:12:16,699
I hope that there's a surprise waiting for us.

356
00:12:17,969 --> 00:12:19,539
- Do we go in?
- Do we just go in?

357
00:12:19,539 --> 00:12:20,539
Okay.

358
00:12:20,539 --> 00:12:21,539
(They had no idea...)

359
00:12:22,169 --> 00:12:25,809
(that this decision would decide their destiny.)

360
00:12:26,909 --> 00:12:28,849
(While the siblings are getting changed)

361
00:12:28,849 --> 00:12:31,349
Before that, we should...

362
00:12:32,519 --> 00:12:35,349
(A suspicious strategy meeting is underway.)

363
00:12:36,049 --> 00:12:37,219
(This boat isn't supposed to be...)

364
00:12:37,219 --> 00:12:39,489
(for a poster photo shoot.)

365
00:12:39,919 --> 00:12:42,729
(The poster the siblings are shooting for is fake.)

366
00:12:43,189 --> 00:12:45,629
(The boat prepared for the photo shoot)

367
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:47,829
(In reality,)

368
00:12:47,829 --> 00:12:50,169
(it's a fishing boat for work.)

369
00:12:51,699 --> 00:12:54,309
(The photographer for the fake poster shoot is ready too.)

370
00:12:54,709 --> 00:12:56,939
The cast is arriving. Please get ready.

371
00:12:57,209 --> 00:12:59,279
(On standby)

372
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:03,249
Gosh. As expected, the sun at the sea...

373
00:13:03,309 --> 00:13:04,819
Did you put the overalls over your pants?

374
00:13:04,819 --> 00:13:06,989
- Yes.
- I took my pants off,

375
00:13:07,519 --> 00:13:08,619
so it's refreshing.

376
00:13:08,919 --> 00:13:11,189
(Laughing)

377
00:13:11,819 --> 00:13:13,089
- Hello.
- Hello.

378
00:13:13,089 --> 00:13:15,129
- Hello.
- Hello.

379
00:13:16,329 --> 00:13:18,499
(Today's unsuspecting targets are entering.)

380
00:13:18,729 --> 00:13:20,199
- Should we go...
- Yes.

381
00:13:20,199 --> 00:13:21,199
- on the boat?
- Do you need a hand?

382
00:13:21,199 --> 00:13:22,229
No, it's okay.

383
00:13:22,229 --> 00:13:23,939
(They board the boat without a single doubt.)

384
00:13:23,939 --> 00:13:25,199
Can you give me a hand?

385
00:13:26,439 --> 00:13:27,509
Heave-ho!

386
00:13:28,309 --> 00:13:30,339
(She steps onto the fishing boat with a powerful cheer.)

387
00:13:30,809 --> 00:13:31,939
The boat is big.

388
00:13:32,939 --> 00:13:34,009
Are we...

389
00:13:34,449 --> 00:13:36,579
- In one line...
- Line up in a single line.

390
00:13:36,849 --> 00:13:38,649
- Jung Ah.
- She's at the center.

391
00:13:39,549 --> 00:13:41,849
(They start with a group photo.)

392
00:13:42,249 --> 00:13:43,719
(Smiling)

393
00:13:43,719 --> 00:13:45,419
(Laughing)

394
00:13:46,389 --> 00:13:49,289
(They continue with the photo shoot completely unaware.)

395
00:13:49,889 --> 00:13:52,059
They're very good. I knew it.

396
00:13:52,299 --> 00:13:53,469
(Trying to set the mood)

397
00:13:54,599 --> 00:13:56,899
(Despite the slightly awkward attempts to build excitement)

398
00:13:57,869 --> 00:14:00,039
(The group photo shoot is completed smoothly.)

399
00:14:00,609 --> 00:14:03,209
Could each of you hold a razor shell?

400
00:14:04,039 --> 00:14:05,039
Yes!

401
00:14:06,039 --> 00:14:07,509
- That's so charismatic.
- Seriously.

402
00:14:08,109 --> 00:14:09,209
Isn't that "Smugglers?"

403
00:14:09,209 --> 00:14:10,479
(Laughing)

404
00:14:11,719 --> 00:14:14,519
(The 2026 version of movie "Smugglers")

405
00:14:14,919 --> 00:14:16,789
Answer the phone with the razor shell.

406
00:14:17,959 --> 00:14:18,959
Hello?

407
00:14:18,959 --> 00:14:20,329
(Answering a call)

408
00:14:20,329 --> 00:14:21,359
Hello?

409
00:14:22,259 --> 00:14:23,259
(Satisfied)

410
00:14:23,559 --> 00:14:25,199
- Yes.
- That's cute.

411
00:14:25,199 --> 00:14:26,229
(I'm in the middle of a shoot, so I'm busy.)

412
00:14:26,629 --> 00:14:28,999
Here we go. One, two, three.

413
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:33,369
(10 minutes before the labor starts)

414
00:14:33,839 --> 00:14:34,869
You look amazing.

415
00:14:34,869 --> 00:14:37,409
The older siblings are done. The younger siblings, come in.

416
00:14:37,409 --> 00:14:39,009
- That was fast.
- Shall I take this?

417
00:14:39,209 --> 00:14:41,649
- We'll do this first.
- After the shoot?

418
00:14:41,909 --> 00:14:42,909
Okay.

419
00:14:42,909 --> 00:14:43,979
- That was...
- Where?

420
00:14:44,519 --> 00:14:45,579
quite simple.

421
00:14:45,579 --> 00:14:47,689
- Please go down.
- Okay.

422
00:14:47,689 --> 00:14:48,849
(Since it's a fake poster photo shoot)

423
00:14:49,319 --> 00:14:52,259
Should I go up? Or do you want to?

424
00:14:52,259 --> 00:14:53,989
- Why don't you go up first?
- You go up.

425
00:14:53,989 --> 00:14:54,989
(Feeling sorry for no reason)

426
00:14:55,629 --> 00:14:57,229
(They're totally ready for the shoot.)

427
00:14:58,429 --> 00:15:00,899
(The youngest members take it too seriously.)

428
00:15:01,369 --> 00:15:02,599
Gosh, look at them.

429
00:15:04,869 --> 00:15:07,109
(A bonus scene for getting the older siblings' attention)

430
00:15:07,439 --> 00:15:08,609
(Laughing)

431
00:15:08,709 --> 00:15:11,839
Yes, that's very cute. You Seok is so cute.

432
00:15:11,839 --> 00:15:13,139
(Playful)

433
00:15:13,309 --> 00:15:14,409
One, two, three.

434
00:15:14,409 --> 00:15:16,849
You Seok is so adorable. My goodness.

435
00:15:18,079 --> 00:15:19,619
(3 minutes before heading out to sea)

436
00:15:20,389 --> 00:15:23,049
These look so fresh.

437
00:15:23,449 --> 00:15:24,959
- I've never touched them live.
- Me neither.

438
00:15:25,689 --> 00:15:27,489
(With their hands full of sea squirts,)

439
00:15:28,959 --> 00:15:31,699
(the youngest ones settle into their seats on the boat.)

440
00:15:33,059 --> 00:15:35,799
Undo the rope, please.

441
00:15:36,299 --> 00:15:37,569
(Rushing)

442
00:15:37,799 --> 00:15:40,439
(The operation begins.)

443
00:15:41,139 --> 00:15:43,409
(Fumbling around)

444
00:15:43,639 --> 00:15:44,879
(Mission complete)

445
00:15:46,079 --> 00:15:49,049
(The hidden camera emerges.)

446
00:15:50,879 --> 00:15:52,049
Lift it up.

447
00:15:52,749 --> 00:15:55,119
Here we go. One, two, three.

448
00:15:55,119 --> 00:15:56,389
(The cameras are set.)

449
00:15:58,719 --> 00:16:00,119
That's very cute.

450
00:16:00,119 --> 00:16:01,789
(Completely unaware of what's about to happen)

451
00:16:02,559 --> 00:16:03,859
- You Seok looks so cute.
- That's cute.

452
00:16:05,329 --> 00:16:06,329
(The engine turns on.)

453
00:16:06,329 --> 00:16:07,629
(Surprised)

454
00:16:09,529 --> 00:16:11,199
(Rumbling)

455
00:16:12,599 --> 00:16:14,339
- What?
- Are we heading out?

456
00:16:15,009 --> 00:16:16,639
- What?
- Are we leaving?

457
00:16:16,639 --> 00:16:18,579
- Why?
- Hold on.

458
00:16:21,209 --> 00:16:22,649
- What?
- Are we leaving?

459
00:16:22,649 --> 00:16:25,049
(The fishing boat sets sail.)

460
00:16:25,379 --> 00:16:27,389
- Why?
- Hold on.

461
00:16:27,889 --> 00:16:29,919
- What's going on?
- What's happening?

462
00:16:30,719 --> 00:16:31,789
What?

463
00:16:32,389 --> 00:16:34,289
(In total panic)

464
00:16:36,559 --> 00:16:38,659
(Even the managers are caught off guard by the sudden departure.)

465
00:16:39,229 --> 00:16:40,599
- What's going on?
- Are they leaving?

466
00:16:41,999 --> 00:16:43,899
(We're leaving.)

467
00:16:45,769 --> 00:16:46,799
- Hey.
- Wait a minute.

468
00:16:47,069 --> 00:16:49,739
- Wait, where's the director?
- Seriously?

469
00:16:49,739 --> 00:16:51,779
- Jung Ah!
- Is this serious?

470
00:16:52,009 --> 00:16:53,009
- Seriously...
- Wait.

471
00:16:53,009 --> 00:16:54,279
What's going on?

472
00:16:54,449 --> 00:16:56,579
- Is this serious?
- Hold on.

473
00:16:56,579 --> 00:16:57,579
Are they leaving?

474
00:16:58,949 --> 00:17:01,089
(The boat slowly drifts farther away from shore.)

475
00:17:01,089 --> 00:17:02,919
- Is this for real?
- Seriously?

476
00:17:02,919 --> 00:17:04,089
(Jung Ah is flustered by the first unexpected situation...)

477
00:17:04,089 --> 00:17:05,259
(on Fresh off the Sea.)

478
00:17:05,359 --> 00:17:06,989
- What?
- Oh, no.

479
00:17:06,989 --> 00:17:08,629
(Oh, no...)

480
00:17:09,059 --> 00:17:10,629
- Please help us.
- Aren't we working together?

481
00:17:10,759 --> 00:17:13,199
I guess you guys are razor shells, and we're sea squirts.

482
00:17:13,969 --> 00:17:15,699
(She still doesn't understand the situation.)

483
00:17:16,069 --> 00:17:17,239
I thought that we were eating.

484
00:17:17,239 --> 00:17:19,669
Jung Ah, we're hungry.

485
00:17:21,609 --> 00:17:24,279
(Setting sail with shouts on an empty stomach)

486
00:17:24,279 --> 00:17:25,339
Wait a minute.

487
00:17:26,109 --> 00:17:27,349
What do we do about them?

488
00:17:28,279 --> 00:17:31,019
What's going on? Where are they going?

489
00:17:31,019 --> 00:17:32,579
What is this? It's so scary.

490
00:17:33,179 --> 00:17:35,019
Gosh, they're so cruel.

491
00:17:38,219 --> 00:17:40,359
- This is so harsh.
- Why...

492
00:17:40,689 --> 00:17:42,059
I forgot that it was a variety show.

493
00:17:42,059 --> 00:17:45,559
We didn't even bring a hat.

494
00:17:45,559 --> 00:17:48,129
We're starting... My hat...

495
00:17:48,129 --> 00:17:50,669
My hat is over there...

496
00:17:51,239 --> 00:17:52,499
(He puts a life jacket on her instead of a hat.)

497
00:17:52,769 --> 00:17:54,109
My hat is over there.

498
00:17:55,839 --> 00:17:59,309
(The boat that kidnapped the youngest ones sets off.)

499
00:18:01,909 --> 00:18:03,249
(Stunned)

500
00:18:03,779 --> 00:18:05,449
(The siblings are unable to overcome the shock.)

501
00:18:05,449 --> 00:18:07,549
This is unbelievable.

502
00:18:07,549 --> 00:18:09,889
What kind of sudden goodbye was that?

503
00:18:10,389 --> 00:18:12,759
- Was the poster shoot a lie?
- Are they really leaving like that?

504
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:13,789
Was the poster shoot a lie?

505
00:18:14,559 --> 00:18:15,959
Jung Ah, the poster shoot was a lie.

506
00:18:16,959 --> 00:18:17,999
What?

507
00:18:17,999 --> 00:18:20,899
I thought the photo shoot was way too simple.

508
00:18:20,899 --> 00:18:23,129
(Shocked)

509
00:18:23,599 --> 00:18:25,399
Then who was the photographer?

510
00:18:25,399 --> 00:18:26,439
That was...

511
00:18:26,439 --> 00:18:28,009
(The photographer for Fresh off the Sea)

512
00:18:28,309 --> 00:18:30,609
Did we do a photo shoot for the poster?

513
00:18:30,609 --> 00:18:33,139
Jung Ah, it will be during the next shoot.

514
00:18:34,149 --> 00:18:35,979
(Unlike the eldest, the second eldest finds it funny.)

515
00:18:36,049 --> 00:18:38,679
Gosh, that's so hilarious.

516
00:18:39,179 --> 00:18:41,319
This is really fun.

517
00:18:41,719 --> 00:18:42,919
It's very funny.

518
00:18:42,919 --> 00:18:45,219
I thought that someone made a mistake...

519
00:18:45,219 --> 00:18:46,759
when the boat started to move.

520
00:18:47,289 --> 00:18:49,159
- That's so funny.
- Seriously.

521
00:18:51,599 --> 00:18:52,899
(Meanwhile, on the boat that kidnapped the youngest ones)

522
00:18:52,899 --> 00:18:55,269
- Jung Ah!
- Seriously...

523
00:18:56,569 --> 00:18:57,639
Sun Young!

524
00:18:58,499 --> 00:19:00,139
- It was so funny...
- I don't see them.

525
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:02,069
I don't see them anymore.

526
00:19:02,769 --> 00:19:04,879
(Exclaiming)

527
00:19:05,239 --> 00:19:06,279
Whatever.

528
00:19:07,579 --> 00:19:08,609
It will work out somehow.

529
00:19:09,509 --> 00:19:11,179
It would've been funnier...

530
00:19:11,179 --> 00:19:13,049
if we jumped off when the engine started.

531
00:19:14,389 --> 00:19:16,519
- We should've jumped off.
- Is that why...

532
00:19:16,519 --> 00:19:18,089
they told us to grab a lot of sea squirt?

533
00:19:18,089 --> 00:19:19,789
- To keep our hands full.
- To keep us from running away.

534
00:19:19,789 --> 00:19:20,829
To keep our hands busy.

535
00:19:20,829 --> 00:19:21,829
(The clues they missed begin to come back to them.)

536
00:19:22,029 --> 00:19:23,029
- You Seok.
- That's also...

537
00:19:23,029 --> 00:19:25,429
It must be the bungalow we chose.

538
00:19:26,159 --> 00:19:28,029
- What was your color?
- It was red.

539
00:19:28,329 --> 00:19:30,029
- No.
- Was yours red?

540
00:19:30,029 --> 00:19:31,099
Was yours yellow?

541
00:19:32,469 --> 00:19:35,209
- Pick the color you want.
- Let's see.

542
00:19:36,139 --> 00:19:37,139
"Fresh off the Sea."

543
00:19:37,139 --> 00:19:40,209
(The siblings chose the rooms in the colors they liked.)

544
00:19:42,179 --> 00:19:44,019
(On the cue card that You Seok took a photo of)

545
00:19:45,179 --> 00:19:47,519
(There was actually a clue to today's fishing trip.)

546
00:19:47,589 --> 00:19:48,619
(Fresh off the Sea)

547
00:19:48,619 --> 00:19:51,289
(Today's fishing job chosen by the youngest ones)

548
00:19:51,289 --> 00:19:53,419
(Sea squirt)

549
00:19:54,259 --> 00:19:57,599
(That's why the youngest ones were kidnapped onto the boat.)

550
00:19:58,659 --> 00:20:01,769
They promised us motion sickness medicine and breakfast,

551
00:20:02,029 --> 00:20:03,069
but we got nothing.

552
00:20:03,799 --> 00:20:05,099
This place is really...

553
00:20:06,899 --> 00:20:07,969
the best.

554
00:20:08,909 --> 00:20:09,939
(Exclaiming)

555
00:20:10,339 --> 00:20:12,679
- You Seok, let's make sure...
- To get revenge.

556
00:20:12,679 --> 00:20:14,909
- to get revenge someday.
- We have to get revenge.

557
00:20:14,909 --> 00:20:17,979
- We really have to.
- I won't...

558
00:20:17,979 --> 00:20:19,419
We can't let this slide.

559
00:20:19,419 --> 00:20:21,849
They completely got us.

560
00:20:22,789 --> 00:20:25,619
(As the youngest ones vow revenge)

561
00:20:25,819 --> 00:20:28,589
(One month later)

562
00:20:28,729 --> 00:20:30,389
(At the Siblings' House)

563
00:20:30,659 --> 00:20:32,399
We've been thinking about it...

564
00:20:32,399 --> 00:20:34,099
ever since we got taken onto the boat.

565
00:20:34,769 --> 00:20:35,769
We can't be the only ones who get fooled.

566
00:20:35,869 --> 00:20:36,929
(Madly determined)

567
00:20:37,199 --> 00:20:38,969
We prepared this for a month.

568
00:20:39,539 --> 00:20:40,709
I will keep trying.

569
00:20:41,509 --> 00:20:43,709
Nobody, nobody, but you

570
00:20:44,339 --> 00:20:47,249
(A revenge drama by the siblings is coming soon.)

571
00:20:50,049 --> 00:20:51,079
An aquaculture farm.

572
00:20:51,079 --> 00:20:52,279
(They arrive at a vast aquaculture farm.)

573
00:20:53,149 --> 00:20:54,889
We must be here. The boat is speeding down.

574
00:20:54,889 --> 00:20:56,819
- Isn't this an aquaculture farm?
- I think so.

575
00:20:58,459 --> 00:21:00,589
(The fishing boat drops anchor.)

576
00:21:00,789 --> 00:21:01,959
(Glancing)

577
00:21:03,259 --> 00:21:05,629
(You Seok takes a look around the farm.)

578
00:21:05,929 --> 00:21:07,029
- Gosh.
- What is it?

579
00:21:07,129 --> 00:21:08,869
- My gosh.
- You startled me.

580
00:21:08,869 --> 00:21:09,929
It's sea squirts.

581
00:21:10,369 --> 00:21:12,169
- Where? I don't see them.
- They're here. Look.

582
00:21:12,739 --> 00:21:15,369
- They're right below here.
- We saw them in photos yesterday.

583
00:21:17,509 --> 00:21:20,139
(Today's job for the siblings, sea squirts)

584
00:21:22,379 --> 00:21:24,219
(Tongyeong, home to the pristine waters of the southern coast)

585
00:21:24,379 --> 00:21:27,689
Tongyeong's waters are clean,

586
00:21:28,519 --> 00:21:32,019
and the surrounding environment provides the perfect conditions.

587
00:21:33,759 --> 00:21:36,589
(Hidden beneath the warm spring sea of Tongyeong)

588
00:21:38,259 --> 00:21:40,769
The best season for sea squirts is from March to May.

589
00:21:40,769 --> 00:21:41,799
(The sea squirt, the harbinger of spring and flower of the sea)

590
00:21:43,599 --> 00:21:45,939
This is when they taste the best.

591
00:21:47,199 --> 00:21:49,809
We harvest about five tons per day.

592
00:21:49,969 --> 00:21:51,709
They are shipped out...

593
00:21:51,939 --> 00:21:53,909
to places like Busan and Incheon.

594
00:21:53,909 --> 00:21:55,279
(They're sent to destinations all across the country.)

595
00:21:57,579 --> 00:21:59,919
(The bright orange sea squirt blossoms are in full bloom.)

596
00:22:01,119 --> 00:22:04,289
(Tongyeong's sea squirt)

597
00:22:04,789 --> 00:22:05,859
Captain.

598
00:22:06,989 --> 00:22:08,229
- Hello.
- Hello.

599
00:22:08,229 --> 00:22:10,289
- You were so quiet until now.
- All right.

600
00:22:10,489 --> 00:22:11,559
What did you come to do today?

601
00:22:11,829 --> 00:22:13,459
- We don't know.
- No one told us.

602
00:22:13,459 --> 00:22:15,669
But you took photos of the sea squirts.

603
00:22:16,099 --> 00:22:17,939
You came to harvest sea squirts today.

604
00:22:17,939 --> 00:22:20,169
You came to harvest them. Hurry and tie your hair.

605
00:22:21,639 --> 00:22:23,869
(A captain with an unusual personality)

606
00:22:24,309 --> 00:22:25,309
My goodness.

607
00:22:25,309 --> 00:22:27,579
(Immediately getting ready for the day's work)

608
00:22:27,909 --> 00:22:29,379
Do we take off all of them?

609
00:22:29,979 --> 00:22:32,479
- You Seok, what do we do?
- Do we take off the entire line?

610
00:22:34,389 --> 00:22:40,019
(Lurking beneath the sea)

611
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:43,999
- There are so many.
- Don't we need more people, sir?

612
00:22:43,999 --> 00:22:46,099
There are four of us.

613
00:22:46,099 --> 00:22:47,699
Four is enough.

614
00:22:48,799 --> 00:22:50,769
(Worried that we won't be able to handle 1 portion each)

615
00:22:50,769 --> 00:22:52,399
- All right, let's do it.
- Will you just stand there?

616
00:22:52,399 --> 00:22:53,539
- Do you need help?
- Hurry up over here.

617
00:22:53,739 --> 00:22:54,839
Okay.

618
00:22:54,839 --> 00:22:56,309
(The youngest members found the perfect captain.)

619
00:22:57,039 --> 00:22:59,109
- Come here. Let me show you.
- Okay.

620
00:23:00,309 --> 00:23:02,579
(The sea squirt pole hanging from the aquaculture lines)

621
00:23:03,149 --> 00:23:05,649
- This is how you undo it.
- Okay.

622
00:23:06,779 --> 00:23:09,289
(The tightly secured sea squirt pole)

623
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:12,559
(Untying the knot)

624
00:23:12,619 --> 00:23:14,459
(Careful not to let it slip)

625
00:23:15,559 --> 00:23:18,159
(The captain's first demonstration for the youngest members)

626
00:23:18,399 --> 00:23:19,459
Hold it tight.

627
00:23:20,359 --> 00:23:23,899
(If you drop the pole, you will lose the sea squirts.)

628
00:23:24,499 --> 00:23:26,669
- This is very heavy.
- Do I hold onto it?

629
00:23:26,669 --> 00:23:28,939
Of course. You have to hold onto three.

630
00:23:29,639 --> 00:23:30,669
You have to hold three of these.

631
00:23:30,979 --> 00:23:32,479
- Lift it.
- It's so heavy.

632
00:23:32,479 --> 00:23:33,779
- How is it possible? Wait.
- Lift it.

633
00:23:33,779 --> 00:23:35,379
- Do it together.
- Do I really have to hold it?

634
00:23:35,379 --> 00:23:36,409
(The reason why You Seok is struggling this much)

635
00:23:36,409 --> 00:23:37,749
(Bending over)

636
00:23:39,479 --> 00:23:42,719
(The weight of just 1 sea squirt pole)

637
00:23:42,849 --> 00:23:45,259
(About 150kg)

638
00:23:49,229 --> 00:23:51,959
(Countless sea squirts hang endlessly down into the sea.)

639
00:23:54,769 --> 00:23:56,699
(The immense weight of the rope leaves him chuckle in disbelief.)

640
00:23:56,699 --> 00:23:57,869
It's really heavy.

641
00:23:58,169 --> 00:23:59,399
Sir, how should we...

642
00:23:59,399 --> 00:24:01,609
Tie two ropes together like this.

643
00:24:01,609 --> 00:24:02,639
I see.

644
00:24:02,639 --> 00:24:04,439
(Tie two ropes, which weigh 300kg, together with a strong line.)

645
00:24:05,279 --> 00:24:06,679
After tying the ropes together...

646
00:24:06,679 --> 00:24:07,779
(Pull the 300kg of sea squirts toward the crane.)

647
00:24:08,879 --> 00:24:11,879
(Next, hook the line onto the crane, and that's it.)

648
00:24:12,219 --> 00:24:13,279
So, I should untie this...

649
00:24:13,449 --> 00:24:15,819
Now, untie the knot like this.

650
00:24:16,619 --> 00:24:18,489
(Yoon Seo observes how the captain unties it.)

651
00:24:18,589 --> 00:24:20,019
(Skillful)

652
00:24:20,889 --> 00:24:22,089
My, you're doing well.

653
00:24:23,989 --> 00:24:25,199
Now, do it again with another rope.

654
00:24:25,859 --> 00:24:26,859
(Captain, the problem is...)

655
00:24:26,859 --> 00:24:28,169
Pull it out this way.

656
00:24:28,169 --> 00:24:29,729
How do I lift this up, Captain?

657
00:24:29,729 --> 00:24:31,199
- Okay. Two, three. Hold it.
- Oh, gosh.

658
00:24:31,369 --> 00:24:32,999
Stop pulling it. Okay.

659
00:24:33,599 --> 00:24:34,739
Hold this, okay?

660
00:24:34,969 --> 00:24:36,739
- Oh, if I hold it...
- If you hold it...

661
00:24:37,339 --> 00:24:38,579
- You should tie these together.
- Tie them together...

662
00:24:38,579 --> 00:24:40,039
and hook the line onto the crane. Is that right?

663
00:24:40,039 --> 00:24:41,179
(The captain and You Seok help her tie them with a line.)

664
00:24:41,179 --> 00:24:42,249
All right.

665
00:24:42,679 --> 00:24:44,049
Hook the line onto the crane.

666
00:24:45,619 --> 00:24:47,519
(Yoon Seo tries to pull the ropes of sea squirts toward the crane.)

667
00:24:47,519 --> 00:24:48,519
Oh, dear.

668
00:24:49,249 --> 00:24:50,689
(Worried)

669
00:24:51,419 --> 00:24:52,419
Oh, gosh.

670
00:24:52,419 --> 00:24:53,619
(She staggers under the weight of the 300kg sea squirt ropes.)

671
00:24:53,989 --> 00:24:55,089
This is insane.

672
00:24:57,599 --> 00:24:58,999
(Letting out a bit of rough language, she succeeds.)

673
00:24:58,999 --> 00:25:00,059
One more time.

674
00:25:00,629 --> 00:25:01,699
One more time.

675
00:25:01,699 --> 00:25:03,329
(She's only done it once, but she's already sweating.)

676
00:25:04,539 --> 00:25:05,899
So this is how sea squirts make it to our dinner tables.

677
00:25:06,669 --> 00:25:08,669
- I didn't know it was so hard.
- I just realized...

678
00:25:08,669 --> 00:25:09,809
that it wasn't easy at all.

679
00:25:10,409 --> 00:25:12,179
- We've only eaten them.
- Right.

680
00:25:12,179 --> 00:25:13,239
(Chuckling)

681
00:25:14,609 --> 00:25:17,519
(Sea squirts keep coming endlessly, leaving them no time to rest.)

682
00:25:19,949 --> 00:25:23,049
(The battle with the sea squirts feels like an actual war.)

683
00:25:23,049 --> 00:25:24,119
It's so heavy.

684
00:25:26,019 --> 00:25:27,189
My knee hurts.

685
00:25:27,489 --> 00:25:29,059
(Groaning)

686
00:25:31,059 --> 00:25:32,259
(Exclaiming in disbelief)

687
00:25:32,259 --> 00:25:34,199
- Oh, gosh.
- Our very first task is not easy.

688
00:25:35,599 --> 00:25:36,669
Hold on.

689
00:25:37,369 --> 00:25:38,899
Seriously, it's still...

690
00:25:38,899 --> 00:25:40,099
(The weight of the sea squirt ropes makes it even harder.)

691
00:25:40,909 --> 00:25:42,839
(Hunching over)

692
00:25:42,839 --> 00:25:43,869
Wait.

693
00:25:44,709 --> 00:25:46,679
This is an absolute backbreaker.

694
00:25:47,779 --> 00:25:49,649
(They continue working in a bent-over position.)

695
00:25:51,049 --> 00:25:52,149
Gosh, my knee hurts.

696
00:25:52,319 --> 00:25:53,949
(It's even more painful since she works on one knee.)

697
00:25:54,149 --> 00:25:55,389
Leave it. And grab this one. Okay.

698
00:25:55,389 --> 00:25:56,619
(It seems like he finally straightens his back.)

699
00:25:57,589 --> 00:25:59,319
(But he staggers under the weight of the 300kg sea squirt ropes.)

700
00:26:00,319 --> 00:26:02,529
(He's hunched over again.)

701
00:26:03,929 --> 00:26:06,929
(It takes him such a long time to reach the crane.)

702
00:26:08,299 --> 00:26:10,729
(He arrived.)

703
00:26:11,239 --> 00:26:12,469
(Groaning)

704
00:26:12,469 --> 00:26:13,899
(You Seok sees Yoon Seo struggling and returns right away.)

705
00:26:13,899 --> 00:26:15,369
(Rushing)

706
00:26:16,139 --> 00:26:17,409
Jung Ah and Sun Young would've...

707
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:18,809
I'm glad we're doing this, not them.

708
00:26:19,209 --> 00:26:21,649
(Maybe it's a relief that they're not the ones doing this.)

709
00:26:22,649 --> 00:26:23,779
(Sighing)

710
00:26:23,849 --> 00:26:24,879
Hold on.

711
00:26:26,879 --> 00:26:28,849
- That's a difficult one.
- Gosh, this knot is...

712
00:26:30,449 --> 00:26:31,559
I made it.

713
00:26:32,259 --> 00:26:35,159
(The dexterous Yoon Seo can untie a difficult knot as well.)

714
00:26:35,459 --> 00:26:36,659
- I'll hold it for you.
- Hold this.

715
00:26:36,659 --> 00:26:38,199
You can let it go.

716
00:26:39,459 --> 00:26:40,499
After that...

717
00:26:40,499 --> 00:26:42,269
(While she's at it, Yoon Seo tries to tie ropes with a line too.)

718
00:26:43,199 --> 00:26:44,269
All right.

719
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:45,469
(Yoon Seo's handwork has become more dazzling.)

720
00:26:45,469 --> 00:26:46,499
Okay.

721
00:26:48,139 --> 00:26:50,539
(Yoon Seo's skills simply amaze You Seok.)

722
00:26:51,139 --> 00:26:52,879
(The youngest members hook the lines on the crane.)

723
00:26:52,879 --> 00:26:54,849
- The crane will haul them out now.
- Show me.

724
00:26:58,279 --> 00:27:00,919
(Exhausted)

725
00:27:00,919 --> 00:27:02,619
Are we going to strip all these off the ropes today?

726
00:27:03,619 --> 00:27:04,759
That's a lot.

727
00:27:06,289 --> 00:27:08,529
(The crane is on.)

728
00:27:09,089 --> 00:27:10,459
(Surprised)

729
00:27:10,459 --> 00:27:11,629
I can't see the end of it.

730
00:27:13,929 --> 00:27:16,569
(The sea squirts are slowly coming up.)

731
00:27:20,139 --> 00:27:21,569
(Surprised)

732
00:27:21,669 --> 00:27:22,709
So we're going to...

733
00:27:22,969 --> 00:27:25,179
- Should we strip them all?
- I can't see the end.

734
00:27:28,509 --> 00:27:29,509
How many... My gosh.

735
00:27:30,149 --> 00:27:31,149
What?

736
00:27:31,149 --> 00:27:33,279
(Sea squirt tower)

737
00:27:34,619 --> 00:27:37,049
(They finally show themselves, coming out of the deep sea.)

738
00:27:39,389 --> 00:27:43,329
(Sea squirts, the flowers of the sea)

739
00:27:47,159 --> 00:27:48,199
My goodness.

740
00:27:48,199 --> 00:27:50,129
(It's taking a while to lift them up with the crane.)

741
00:27:51,099 --> 00:27:52,799
(Now it makes sense why they felt so heavy.)

742
00:27:54,369 --> 00:27:55,609
- You Seok.
- Move out of the way.

743
00:27:55,609 --> 00:27:57,169
(The sea squirt tower weighing 1.8 tons)

744
00:27:57,169 --> 00:27:58,209
You Seok, move aside.

745
00:27:58,209 --> 00:27:59,379
No, wait.

746
00:28:00,209 --> 00:28:01,209
No, wait.

747
00:28:01,209 --> 00:28:04,209
(The sea squirt tower)

748
00:28:07,419 --> 00:28:08,419
- My gosh.
- Oh, my.

749
00:28:08,419 --> 00:28:09,719
(Shocked)

750
00:28:10,189 --> 00:28:11,389
- Where should I go?
- It's huge.

751
00:28:13,189 --> 00:28:14,219
Oh, gosh.

752
00:28:14,219 --> 00:28:15,689
(Stretching 6m long, it's an overwhelmingly massive sight.)

753
00:28:17,189 --> 00:28:18,599
They look like alien tentacles.

754
00:28:20,029 --> 00:28:21,469
Look at them shooting water.

755
00:28:25,599 --> 00:28:28,639
(The sea squirts are shooting the sea water.)

756
00:28:30,939 --> 00:28:32,579
I've never seen so many sea squirts in one place before.

757
00:28:33,609 --> 00:28:34,979
It feels like CGI.

758
00:28:36,649 --> 00:28:37,679
(The reason why sea squirts are called the flowers of the sea)

759
00:28:37,679 --> 00:28:39,279
It looks like a flower garden of sea squirts.

760
00:28:40,149 --> 00:28:42,019
- Should we hook more of them?
- Yes, keep going.

761
00:28:42,019 --> 00:28:43,189
- Should we hook more of them?
- Yes.

762
00:28:43,189 --> 00:28:44,289
Oh, we should do it again?

763
00:28:44,289 --> 00:28:45,589
(Round 2 begins right away.)

764
00:28:46,059 --> 00:28:48,529
Yes, Captain. Got it.

765
00:28:48,529 --> 00:28:49,929
- Let's begin.
- We're doing it again right away.

766
00:28:51,029 --> 00:28:52,859
I wonder what Jung Ah and Sun Young are doing now.

767
00:28:53,699 --> 00:28:54,729
What do you think, You Seok?

768
00:28:54,729 --> 00:28:57,169
(At the same time, the older members who were separated from them...)

769
00:28:58,069 --> 00:29:00,669
(At the same time, at the bungalow)

770
