Are you sure you didn't learn this?

1778
01:09:14,065 --> 01:09:16,295
- You have good taste.
- I didn't learn at all.

1779
01:09:16,635 --> 01:09:19,035
You have an eye for arranging them.

1780
01:09:19,035 --> 01:09:20,075
I don't.

1781
01:09:20,075 --> 01:09:21,135
(Laughing)

1782
01:09:21,135 --> 01:09:23,375
- You have good taste...
- Those who do flower arrangement...

1783
01:09:23,375 --> 01:09:25,475
- in aesthetics.
- would laugh at it.

1784
01:09:28,375 --> 01:09:30,615
(As he stares blankly at Jung Ah's flower arrangement...)

1785
01:09:34,515 --> 01:09:36,355
(He's starting to get bored.)

1786
01:09:38,285 --> 01:09:39,725
Shall we go ride a luge?

1787
01:09:40,125 --> 01:09:41,695
- Do you have money?
- We don't.

1788
01:09:41,695 --> 01:09:42,995
- We have five dollars left.
- We don't have money.

1789
01:09:44,495 --> 01:09:47,165
I want to ride a luge and a cable car.

1790
01:09:47,165 --> 01:09:48,635
Since we came all the way to Tongyeong.

1791
01:09:49,765 --> 01:09:51,535
That was such a mind-blowing question.

1792
01:09:51,535 --> 01:09:52,635
"Do you have money?"

1793
01:09:53,505 --> 01:09:54,575
(Humble)

1794
01:09:54,575 --> 01:09:56,745
What labor will we get to do tomorrow?

1795
01:09:56,745 --> 01:09:58,605
That question made me feel so small.

1796
01:09:58,745 --> 01:09:59,805
"Do you have money?"

1797
01:10:00,845 --> 01:10:01,915
I don't.

1798
01:10:04,685 --> 01:10:05,785
For now...

1799
01:10:05,785 --> 01:10:06,985
(Meanwhile, Sun Young is making cold coffee.)

1800
01:10:07,755 --> 01:10:12,025
Let's make Jung Ah's first.

1801
01:10:13,125 --> 01:10:15,895
(Special note: She loves Jung Ah so much.)

1802
01:10:16,625 --> 01:10:17,795
Is it too strong?

1803
01:10:19,065 --> 01:10:20,065
Jung Ah.

1804
01:10:20,065 --> 01:10:21,065
(She calls Jung Ah immediately.)

1805
01:10:21,065 --> 01:10:22,435
Try it first.

1806
01:10:23,605 --> 01:10:24,935
Shall I make it milder?

1807
01:10:24,935 --> 01:10:26,165
- This is just nice.
- Is it okay?

1808
01:10:26,165 --> 01:10:27,505
Thank you.

1809
01:10:28,705 --> 01:10:29,775
Sun Young.

1810
01:10:30,605 --> 01:10:31,805
This is crazy.

1811
01:10:32,075 --> 01:10:33,375
It taste better than the ones they sell in coffee shops.

1812
01:10:34,245 --> 01:10:35,875
I'll have instant coffee.

1813
01:10:35,875 --> 01:10:37,845
- Instant coffee?
- I really shouldn't, though.

1814
01:10:37,845 --> 01:10:39,045
I already had two today.

1815
01:10:39,245 --> 01:10:40,285
- I'll have one more.
- Sun Young.

1816
01:10:40,285 --> 01:10:41,385
Let me just have one more.

1817
01:10:41,385 --> 01:10:43,885
- But it...
- This is why I can't lose weight.

1818
01:10:44,385 --> 01:10:46,155
Isn't it so nice and sweet?

1819
01:10:46,185 --> 01:10:47,395
That's true.

1820
01:10:48,595 --> 01:10:49,725
(But...)

1821
01:10:49,725 --> 01:10:50,865
(there's no hot water.)

1822
01:10:50,865 --> 01:10:52,195
There's no water. It's okay.

1823
01:10:52,365 --> 01:10:54,335
- Should I teach you the way?
- What is it?

1824
01:10:54,435 --> 01:10:57,435
When you want to make coffee...

1825
01:10:57,435 --> 01:11:00,735
but there's no water... You hear the sound?

1826
01:11:00,735 --> 01:11:02,135
It's heated up.

1827
01:11:02,575 --> 01:11:03,945
- Like this.
- What?

1828
01:11:04,075 --> 01:11:05,245
It's heated up.

1829
01:11:05,245 --> 01:11:06,575
- Look, Yoon Seo.
- Sun Young.

1830
01:11:06,575 --> 01:11:08,045
Look, Yoon Seo. Just like that.

1831
01:11:09,115 --> 01:11:10,785
Isn't it fascinating? You don't need to boil it.

1832
01:11:11,815 --> 01:11:12,915
You didn't know, did you?

1833
01:11:13,515 --> 01:11:14,885
Because the pot is still hot.

1834
01:11:15,985 --> 01:11:17,725
Is this funny?

1835
01:11:17,955 --> 01:11:19,255
If it doesn't make the sound, it means it doesn't work anymore.

1836
01:11:19,385 --> 01:11:21,625
What's so funny about this?

1837
01:11:21,895 --> 01:11:23,325
Yoon Seo.

1838
01:11:23,325 --> 01:11:25,565
I've kept this secret for 50 years.

1839
01:11:25,565 --> 01:11:26,935
Exactly. What a secret.

1840
01:11:27,535 --> 01:11:28,565
(Laughing)

1841
01:11:28,565 --> 01:11:29,665
Sun Young.

1842
01:11:29,665 --> 01:11:32,905
It's because I already feel so close to you.

1843
01:11:33,575 --> 01:11:35,675
- We've grown too close.
- You saying silly things?

1844
01:11:35,675 --> 01:11:36,675
Yes.

1845
01:11:36,675 --> 01:11:37,705
(Meanwhile, You Seok...)

1846
01:11:37,705 --> 01:11:38,705
(Groaning)

1847
01:11:38,975 --> 01:11:40,075
(Grunting)

1848
01:11:41,045 --> 01:11:42,075
(Glancing)

1849
01:11:43,375 --> 01:11:45,585
The camera follows me to my sleep.

1850
01:11:46,285 --> 01:11:48,985
(Feeling self-conscious...)

1851
01:11:49,055 --> 01:11:51,155
(or not.)

1852
01:11:52,625 --> 01:11:58,365
(The aftermath of the first labor rushes to him when he lies down.)

1853
01:12:00,365 --> 01:12:02,165
I hope it rains.

1854
01:12:02,265 --> 01:12:03,495
Rain?

1855
01:12:04,335 --> 01:12:07,005
Jung Ah wants to work, basically.

1856
01:12:07,275 --> 01:12:10,875
Sitting around doing nothing tires me out.

1857
01:12:11,405 --> 01:12:13,945
I need to be always doing something.

1858
01:12:15,415 --> 01:12:21,185
(Doing something 1. Standing up and singing)

1859
01:12:21,685 --> 01:12:23,985
(Doing something 2. Looking at the mirror)

1860
01:12:23,985 --> 01:12:26,555
If you give me free time, I spend all of it looking in the mirror.

1861
01:12:27,295 --> 01:12:28,725
(My dear)

1862
01:12:28,725 --> 01:12:30,665
(Don't do anything)

1863
01:12:30,665 --> 01:12:31,895
Isn't it "don't worry about anything?"

1864
01:12:31,995 --> 01:12:33,465
I'll start on another pitch.

1865
01:12:33,465 --> 01:12:34,635
(Please don't do anything)

1866
01:12:35,865 --> 01:12:38,105
- Don't worry about anything.
- Don't do anything?

1867
01:12:38,765 --> 01:12:39,805
See you.

1868
01:12:41,875 --> 01:12:43,905
We'll catch a lot of fish using the fish trap.

1869
01:12:43,905 --> 01:12:44,945
We're off.

1870
01:12:45,205 --> 01:12:46,275
Is that your hat?

1871
01:12:46,975 --> 01:12:47,975
- What?
- Is that your hat?

1872
01:12:48,075 --> 01:12:49,815
- Yes. You Seok...
- I don't have any.

1873
01:12:49,815 --> 01:12:52,215
- Jung Ah.
- You can't put sunscreen like that.

1874
01:12:52,215 --> 01:12:53,385
How else do I apply it?

1875
01:12:53,385 --> 01:12:54,885
- That's horrible.
- Her hat matches well...

1876
01:12:54,885 --> 01:12:56,415
with your outfit.

1877
01:12:56,415 --> 01:12:58,585
You Seok, do that while looking in the mirror.

1878
01:13:00,295 --> 01:13:01,295
I mean...

1879
01:13:03,795 --> 01:13:05,665
Are you going to play golf? My goodness.

1880
01:13:05,825 --> 01:13:07,495
(Laughing)

1881
01:13:08,065 --> 01:13:11,805
(Tapping)

1882
01:13:12,405 --> 01:13:14,675
(While You Seok melts the sunscreen, Yoon Seo prepares the fish trap.)

1883
01:13:15,435 --> 01:13:17,005
- Sun Young.
- Yes?

1884
01:13:17,505 --> 01:13:19,105
After we set up the fish trap,

1885
01:13:19,645 --> 01:13:20,715
let's go on a drive.

1886
01:13:20,945 --> 01:13:22,115
- A drive?
- Yes.

1887
01:13:23,275 --> 01:13:25,545
- Not with a car.
- Then with a motorcycle?

1888
01:13:26,045 --> 01:13:27,055
Bicycle?

1889
01:13:27,355 --> 01:13:28,715
You haven't been on the boat yet.

1890
01:13:29,485 --> 01:13:31,355
- You should get a boat ride today.
- A drive on a boat?

1891
01:13:31,355 --> 01:13:33,455
- Please get ready.
- That sounds good. Okay.

1892
01:13:33,455 --> 01:13:34,555
For now...

1893
01:13:34,555 --> 01:13:35,625
- Salute.
- You don't want to go out?

1894
01:13:35,625 --> 01:13:38,625
- Today...
- I do. I've been dreaming about it.

1895
01:13:39,395 --> 01:13:40,465
See you later, Sun Young.

1896
01:13:41,065 --> 01:13:42,395
- Salute.
- Are you okay?

1897
01:13:42,395 --> 01:13:43,465
Yes.

1898
01:13:43,635 --> 01:13:45,005
- Jung Ah.
- Yes?

1899
01:13:45,105 --> 01:13:46,935
When they come back from setting up the fish trap,

1900
01:13:47,535 --> 01:13:48,605
they want to ride bikes.

1901
01:13:49,805 --> 01:13:50,845
They want to go on a bike ride.

1902
01:13:51,445 --> 01:13:52,445
- Really?
- Yes.

1903
01:13:53,775 --> 01:13:54,975
- Have you used this trap before?
- No.

1904
01:13:55,515 --> 01:13:57,445
I only did it when I was young, so I don't remember clearly.

1905
01:13:58,185 --> 01:14:00,245
- Do we have bait?
- It's inside here.

1906
01:14:00,245 --> 01:14:02,855
There are meat and fish.

1907
01:14:02,855 --> 01:14:04,225
- Okay.
- Which one do you want?

1908
01:14:04,325 --> 01:14:07,355
- I want meat.
- Then I'll use fish bait.

1909
01:14:07,555 --> 01:14:08,655
Let's see which one catches more.

1910
01:14:09,655 --> 01:14:11,495
This path is so cute.

1911
01:14:12,495 --> 01:14:15,395
We're at our sea again

1912
01:14:15,995 --> 01:14:18,565
(The path to the sea became more familiar.)

1913
01:14:19,235 --> 01:14:21,075
I love this kind of nature. It's fascinating.

1914
01:14:21,975 --> 01:14:25,575
(Surrounded by the mysterious and endless nature)

1915
01:14:25,745 --> 01:14:26,745
It smells like the sea.

1916
01:14:26,745 --> 01:14:28,545
(A beginner's guide to life in a fishing village: Trap fishing)

1917
01:14:28,545 --> 01:14:30,245
- If one of us catches more, - Who catches more?

1918
01:14:30,245 --> 01:14:32,885
- let's make...
- The loser goes in the water?

1919
01:14:33,315 --> 01:14:34,485
Why do you keep talking about that?

1920
01:14:36,215 --> 01:14:38,855
- What will the loser do?
- You want to go in the water?

1921
01:14:39,485 --> 01:14:41,155
(The trap fishing siblings settle down at the pier.)

1922
01:14:41,155 --> 01:14:42,195
Isn't it nice?

1923
01:14:42,195 --> 01:14:43,225
(The trap fishing siblings settle down at the pier.)

1924
01:14:43,425 --> 01:14:44,465
Oh, my.

1925
01:14:44,665 --> 01:14:45,695
(Sniffing the fish bait)

1926
01:14:45,695 --> 01:14:46,765
I don't even know how to do it.

1927
01:14:47,295 --> 01:14:48,335
It doesn't smell that bad.

1928
01:14:49,235 --> 01:14:51,635
It needs to smell stronger. That's how it attracts more fish.

1929
01:14:52,565 --> 01:14:53,565
I'll put in as much as possible.

1930
01:14:53,565 --> 01:14:54,775
(The trap fishing beginner is fully focused.)

1931
01:14:55,575 --> 01:14:58,145
We get to do everything possible at the sea.

1932
01:14:58,645 --> 01:14:59,675
Right.

1933
01:15:00,475 --> 01:15:01,645
(The next task is writing wishes on the fish trap.)

1934
01:15:01,645 --> 01:15:02,645
"Yoon Seo."

1935
01:15:03,015 --> 01:15:04,345
"Fresh off the Sea becomes..."

1936
01:15:04,885 --> 01:15:06,615
"a huge hit."

1937
01:15:08,455 --> 01:15:09,585
"Hope it catches a lot."

1938
01:15:10,355 --> 01:15:12,185
(Carefully pouring their wishes into every word)

1939
01:15:12,485 --> 01:15:13,485
Do you see it clearly?

1940
01:15:15,525 --> 01:15:19,065
(Carefully tying to the trap to deliver it to the Sea King)

1941
01:15:19,065 --> 01:15:20,165
Do we tie this to the fish trap?

1942
01:15:20,465 --> 01:15:22,435
- All right. Are you ready, Yoon?
- Are you done?

1943
01:15:22,835 --> 01:15:23,905
I'm ready, Seok.

1944
01:15:25,705 --> 01:15:27,975
Do I go first? You go first.

1945
01:15:29,335 --> 01:15:31,145
- I haven't done it before.
- This is...

1946
01:15:35,115 --> 01:15:37,385
I hope that it catches something so that we can eat.

1947
01:15:37,815 --> 01:15:40,385
(Yoon Seo also throws it hard like You Seok.)

1948
01:15:41,585 --> 01:15:44,055
(A refreshing fish trap dive)

1949
01:15:45,125 --> 01:15:46,255
I hope we catch a lot.

1950
01:15:46,255 --> 01:15:48,855
(What kind of friends will show up in the youngest members' trap?)

1951
01:15:49,525 --> 01:15:50,625
It's beautiful.

1952
01:15:51,325 --> 01:15:52,625
It's drawn with acrylic painting.

1953
01:15:53,965 --> 01:15:55,565
It's called Sopo Village.

1954
01:15:56,195 --> 01:15:58,265
Why Sopo Village? Does it mean a lot of packages come here?

1955
01:16:00,065 --> 01:16:01,135
What does "Sopo" mean?

1956
01:16:01,135 --> 01:16:02,575
(What does "Sopo" mean?)

1957
01:16:03,635 --> 01:16:04,675
I thought I misheard you.

1958
01:16:05,545 --> 01:16:06,545
My goodness.

1959
01:16:08,845 --> 01:16:11,185
(Meanwhile, the siblings are preparing for a mysterious drive.)

1960
01:16:12,345 --> 01:16:15,285
Aren't I wearing too many colors?

1961
01:16:15,285 --> 01:16:17,225
- You look beautiful.
- Do I look okay?

1962
01:16:17,225 --> 01:16:18,225
Okay.

1963
01:16:18,885 --> 01:16:20,385
You should keep your neck warm.

1964
01:16:21,195 --> 01:16:22,525
(And the most excited...)

1965
01:16:23,625 --> 01:16:25,095
(mastermind behind the drive)

1966
01:16:25,795 --> 01:16:28,395
(Carefully choosing the perfect pair of sunglasses)

1967
01:16:30,805 --> 01:16:32,605
(When is he coming out?)

1968
01:16:33,565 --> 01:16:34,735
Shall we listen to some music?

1969
01:16:35,935 --> 01:16:37,405
(Playing the Top 100 hits to raise the energy)

1970
01:16:38,445 --> 01:16:39,505
I like that.

1971
01:16:43,515 --> 01:16:45,285
(Dancing immediately to a song that she recognizes)

1972
01:16:49,855 --> 01:16:51,425
What is she saying?

1973
01:16:51,985 --> 01:16:54,795
For you guys, the lyrics might sound like an alien language.

1974
01:16:54,795 --> 01:16:55,895
- Who is it?
- I don't know.

1975
01:16:56,195 --> 01:16:57,265
It's an idol group.

1976
01:16:57,265 --> 01:16:58,325
Zero, zero.

1977
01:16:59,795 --> 01:17:01,065
(Music is all about the spirit.)

1978
01:17:02,095 --> 01:17:06,705
(No idea what they're singing, but just dance along)

1979
01:17:07,035 --> 01:17:08,375
Moving around makes my back hurt less.

1980
01:17:10,105 --> 01:17:11,175
This is nice.

1981
01:17:11,675 --> 01:17:14,075
(As they dance with excitement)

1982
01:17:15,275 --> 01:17:16,345
It's the sea.

1983
01:17:17,915 --> 01:17:20,245
- We're here.
- Thank you for driving.

1984
01:17:20,245 --> 01:17:21,755
(They arrive at the port.)

1985
01:17:22,255 --> 01:17:23,985
It must be that type of boat.

1986
01:17:23,985 --> 01:17:25,025
(What will be today's ride for the four siblings?)

1987
01:17:25,285 --> 01:17:26,885
(An outboard motor boat to roam the waters of Tongyeong)

1988
01:17:27,295 --> 01:17:29,095
(Simple and easy to operate)

1989
01:17:29,725 --> 01:17:31,995
(Anyone with a driver's license can operate it without any certificate.)

1990
01:17:32,895 --> 01:17:34,665
(Not only can you cruise the waters of Tongyeong by yourself)

1991
01:17:37,605 --> 01:17:40,005
(Self-driving boats are also popular among those who enjoy boat fishing.)

1992
01:17:41,635 --> 01:17:42,675
- Is this it?
- Yes.

1993
01:17:44,305 --> 01:17:45,605
(Getting on first quickly,)

1994
01:17:47,075 --> 01:17:48,875
(the 3rd eldest escorts the eldest aboard 1st.)

1995
01:17:49,745 --> 01:17:50,915
- Gosh.
- Thank you.

1996
01:17:51,515 --> 01:17:53,745
- I like your socks.
- Thank you.

1997
01:17:54,155 --> 01:17:55,985
- Thank you, Mr. Driver.
- I'll try driving it.

1998
01:17:55,985 --> 01:17:56,985
(Today's captain You Seok takes a seat.)

1999
01:17:56,985 --> 01:17:58,125
- You Seok.
- Yes?

2000
01:17:58,225 --> 01:17:59,685
We should take a photo of You Seok.

2001
01:18:00,355 --> 01:18:03,425
My gosh. This is amazing.

2002
01:18:04,865 --> 01:18:07,365
- You Seok, take this.
- I don't want medicine.

2003
01:18:07,795 --> 01:18:08,795
- Go on and take it.
- I'm a man.

2004
01:18:09,395 --> 01:18:11,605
- I don't take medicine.
- What if you throw up later?

2005
01:18:11,605 --> 01:18:13,975
- What is it?
- He's a man, so he won't take it.

2006
01:18:14,375 --> 01:18:15,505
- What medicine is it?
- Motion sickness medicine.

2007
01:18:15,805 --> 01:18:16,805
- Motion sickness medicine?
- Yes.

2008
01:18:17,745 --> 01:18:19,375
(A real man on a boat doesn't need medicine.)

2009
01:18:19,375 --> 01:18:20,505
I don't take motion sickness pills.

2010
01:18:22,745 --> 01:18:23,745
I never get seasick.

2011
01:18:23,745 --> 01:18:25,945
(A captain with serious confidence in his sea legs)

2012
01:18:26,185 --> 01:18:28,785
- I'll show you how to operate it.
- Okay.

2013
01:18:29,085 --> 01:18:32,485
When you use it, you need to lower the engine first.

2014
01:18:32,685 --> 01:18:35,055
You must lower it. There's a button here.

2015
01:18:35,425 --> 01:18:37,425
- Press the lower one.
- It's going down.

2016
01:18:37,525 --> 01:18:38,565
You have to lower the engine.

2017
01:18:39,325 --> 01:18:40,325
- That's it.
- Yes.

2018
01:18:40,525 --> 01:18:43,195
Press down and move forward to advance.

2019
01:18:43,195 --> 01:18:45,805
- Lower it to move back.
- Lower it all the way to move back.

2020
01:18:46,865 --> 01:18:47,875
(It's very easy.)

2021
01:18:48,835 --> 01:18:49,875
I got it.

2022
01:18:49,875 --> 01:18:51,645
(Mastered it perfectly just in 1 minute)

2023
01:18:52,145 --> 01:18:54,175
Is everyone ready?

2024
01:18:54,545 --> 01:18:56,615
- Yes, let's go.
- Please set out.

2025
01:18:56,615 --> 01:18:57,945
- We're ready.
- We're ready.

2026
01:18:58,545 --> 01:18:59,585
(Then we'll depart.)

2027
01:18:59,585 --> 01:19:01,415
(Click)

2028
01:19:02,085 --> 01:19:03,285
See you in a while.

2029
01:19:03,285 --> 01:19:04,355
(It was carried out safely with all cast wearing...)

2030
01:19:04,355 --> 01:19:05,425
(life jackets and following safety protocols.)

2031
01:19:06,185 --> 01:19:08,925
(The outboard boat slowly begins to move.)

2032
01:19:09,455 --> 01:19:10,525
Keep turning.

2033
01:19:10,525 --> 01:19:13,595
(Towards the sea)

2034
01:19:14,635 --> 01:19:17,095
- Is it similar to driving a car?
- I think so.

2035
01:19:17,095 --> 01:19:18,935
(Advancing smoothly)

2036
01:19:19,465 --> 01:19:22,475
- Is it like driving a car?
- It is,

2037
01:19:22,805 --> 01:19:24,675
but you have to use both hands.

2038
01:19:24,675 --> 01:19:26,305
You have to use both hands?

2039
01:19:27,745 --> 01:19:30,275
(I will still give you a nice ride.)

2040
01:19:31,815 --> 01:19:33,285
(Bold and confident steering)

2041
01:19:33,815 --> 01:19:36,485
Gosh, the sunlight is intense.

2042
01:19:36,585 --> 01:19:39,255
(Racing toward the waters of Tongyeong)

2043
01:19:40,455 --> 01:19:42,925
(The siblings' outboard boat smoothly glides across the sea.)

2044
01:19:43,495 --> 01:19:45,895
(This is exciting.)

2045
01:19:46,495 --> 01:19:47,565
I like it.

2046
01:19:47,865 --> 01:19:50,435
It feels like we're floating on water because it sits low.

2047
01:19:50,435 --> 01:19:51,465
This is nice.

2048
01:19:52,035 --> 01:19:53,205
Hello!

2049
01:19:54,075 --> 01:19:57,105
(A completely different view of the sea from when they're working)

2050
01:19:58,175 --> 01:19:59,175
This is fun.

2051
01:19:59,175 --> 01:20:00,505
(A perfectly healing ride that won their hearts)

2052
01:20:01,375 --> 01:20:03,345
Girls, why don't we take a photo?

2053
01:20:03,845 --> 01:20:04,845
One, two, three.

2054
01:20:04,845 --> 01:20:07,515
(A commemorative photo cannot be missed.)

2055
01:20:08,085 --> 01:20:10,655
I feel like we're the only ones here.

2056
01:20:10,655 --> 01:20:12,925
- It's so beautiful.
- I feel like I'm rich.

2057
01:20:13,485 --> 01:20:15,655
- I feel like...
- Like we're on a yacht.

2058
01:20:16,125 --> 01:20:18,425
(A moment that rivals the luxury of any yacht)

2059
01:20:22,295 --> 01:20:23,665
The weather is so beautiful.

2060
01:20:24,765 --> 01:20:26,865
(After cruising for a while, the captain relaxes.)

2061
01:20:28,535 --> 01:20:29,575
Nice.

2062
01:20:31,145 --> 01:20:33,745
What's today's sailing route?

2063
01:20:34,275 --> 01:20:36,845
Do you see that white lighthouse over there?

2064
01:20:36,845 --> 01:20:38,985
- Yes.
- We're heading there.

2065
01:20:38,985 --> 01:20:40,045
Okay.

2066
01:20:40,045 --> 01:20:41,285
We're heading there.

2067
01:20:41,285 --> 01:20:42,355
(Why is he talking like that?)

2068
01:20:42,355 --> 01:20:44,025
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

2069
01:20:44,025 --> 01:20:45,585
If you're ready, scream.

2070
01:20:45,585 --> 01:20:46,685
(Screaming)

2071
01:20:47,955 --> 01:20:49,025
(They love it.)

2072
01:20:49,125 --> 01:20:50,225
You've done this before, haven't you?

2073
01:20:51,225 --> 01:20:53,125
You Seok, you sound like a real captain.

2074
01:20:53,125 --> 01:20:54,165
(The captain's way of speaking feels strangely familiar.)

2075
01:20:54,165 --> 01:20:56,865
- Actually, he was a captain.
- He really was.

2076
01:20:57,265 --> 01:20:58,935
I had a captain's spirit inside me.

2077
01:20:58,935 --> 01:20:59,935
(I didn't know about it.)

2078
01:21:01,375 --> 01:21:02,805
(I, Kang You Seok)

2079
01:21:02,805 --> 01:21:05,005
(My captain's spirit is rising.)

2080
01:21:05,875 --> 01:21:09,375
(A true man of the sea, at his best on the boat)

2081
01:21:10,715 --> 01:21:12,345
The boat is quite stable.

2082
01:21:12,345 --> 01:21:13,985
(Steady and unwavering, in charge of today's voyage)

2083
01:21:13,985 --> 01:21:15,585
(I'm Captain Kang, the master of the sea.)

2084
01:21:16,085 --> 01:21:18,755
(His jacket is puffed up as much as his confidence.)

2085
01:21:19,085 --> 01:21:20,085
You can count on me.

2086
01:21:20,085 --> 01:21:21,955
(You can count on me.)

2087
01:21:22,925 --> 01:21:23,925
My goodness.

2088
01:21:23,925 --> 01:21:26,125
(His enthusiastic fans appear.)

2089
01:21:26,125 --> 01:21:28,735
The wind... Captain, could you turn around?

2090
01:21:30,135 --> 01:21:32,265
Oh, my.

2091
01:21:32,705 --> 01:21:33,965
The weather is really beautiful.

2092
01:21:33,965 --> 01:21:35,005
(Captain Kang knows how to treat his fans.)

2093
01:21:35,405 --> 01:21:38,075
Captain, you're taking the longer route...

2094
01:21:38,075 --> 01:21:39,945
because we're so pretty, right?

2095
01:21:39,945 --> 01:21:42,275
Normally, I would've returned a long time ago.

2096
01:21:43,275 --> 01:21:44,815
I don't even work this late.

2097
01:21:44,815 --> 01:21:45,885
(Encouraged by the positive reaction, he got more smug.)

2098
01:21:46,385 --> 01:21:49,555
Captain, where do you live?

2099
01:21:50,515 --> 01:21:52,825
The entire Tongyeong is my home.

2100
01:21:52,985 --> 01:21:54,625
(Cheeky)

2101
01:21:54,725 --> 01:21:55,925
He's really good.

2102
01:21:56,655 --> 01:21:58,025
He suddenly got the hang of it.

2103
01:21:58,025 --> 01:21:59,325
(A man who's almost too perfect as a captain)

2104
01:21:59,425 --> 01:22:03,165
Captain, I bet you were very popular when you were young.

2105
01:22:03,635 --> 01:22:04,835
Back in my day...

2106
01:22:04,835 --> 01:22:06,065
(Groaning)

2107
01:22:06,405 --> 01:22:08,105
People lined up just to get on my boat.

2108
01:22:08,105 --> 01:22:10,435
(A handsome captain who had countless women swooning)

2109
01:22:10,435 --> 01:22:11,545
They practically lined up.

2110
01:22:11,545 --> 01:22:12,545
(My goodness)

2111
01:22:14,545 --> 01:22:16,045
- Look how shameless he is.
- I think...

2112
01:22:16,515 --> 01:22:19,845
He used his boat to charm women.

2113
01:22:20,885 --> 01:22:22,155
Gosh, he's turning.

2114
01:22:22,155 --> 01:22:23,215
(I'm feeling good. Let's kick it up a notch.)

2115
01:22:23,655 --> 01:22:27,755
(The rugged man of the sea makes a turn to show off.)

2116
01:22:28,295 --> 01:22:31,725
(A complete 180 from the start, charging ahead at full speed)

2117
01:22:33,995 --> 01:22:35,235
It's the white lighthouse.

2118
01:22:38,105 --> 01:22:41,275
(While cruising the sea with the captain)

2119
01:22:42,005 --> 01:22:43,335
(they already reached their destination.)

2120
01:22:45,175 --> 01:22:46,475
Captain, are you going to turn around?

2121
01:22:46,475 --> 01:22:47,845
(Disappointed)

2122
01:22:48,575 --> 01:22:49,845
Reversing.

2123
01:22:51,045 --> 01:22:52,045
(Putting it in reverse)

2124
01:22:54,515 --> 01:22:56,115
(The cheers of fangirls echo across the Tongyeong sea.)

2125
01:22:56,115 --> 01:22:57,115
- My goodness.
- Gosh.

2126
01:22:57,115 --> 01:22:58,925
- Are you having fun?
- Yes.

2127
01:22:59,485 --> 01:23:01,355
No, please!

2128
01:23:01,355 --> 01:23:02,395
Gosh.

2129
01:23:02,395 --> 01:23:03,725
(A wild U-turn)

2130
01:23:04,195 --> 01:23:05,225
My goodness.

2131
01:23:05,225 --> 01:23:06,665
- No, mister.
- That's cold.

2132
01:23:06,665 --> 01:23:08,595
(A port turn that makes the ladies' hearts race)

2133
01:23:08,595 --> 01:23:09,895
Shall we go fast?

2134
01:23:10,935 --> 01:23:13,305
(Giggling)

2135
01:23:13,505 --> 01:23:16,075
Captain, you're the best.

2136
01:23:16,235 --> 01:23:17,575
How about one more ride?

2137
01:23:18,145 --> 01:23:19,145
Yes.

2138
01:23:19,145 --> 01:23:22,375
(The devoted fans are absolutely thrilled.)

2139
01:23:22,975 --> 01:23:26,415
Captain, will you do this for us again next year?

2140
01:23:26,415 --> 01:23:27,985
Come back tomorrow. I'll give you another ride.

2141
01:23:27,985 --> 01:23:29,085
(Next year is too far away.)

2142
01:23:29,085 --> 01:23:31,025
Tomorrow, it will be free.

2143
01:23:33,085 --> 01:23:34,725
(The ladies go wild over the VIP treatment on their return visit.)

2144
01:23:34,925 --> 01:23:37,355
Captain, you need to make money too.

2145
01:23:37,355 --> 01:23:39,025
When I give a ride to pretty ladies,

2146
01:23:39,165 --> 01:23:40,665
I feel good even if I don't make money.

2147
01:23:41,495 --> 01:23:43,435
(The more they get to know him, the more he's their type.)

2148
01:23:43,595 --> 01:23:47,105
Captain, we're having sea squirt doenjang jjigae...

2149
01:23:47,105 --> 01:23:49,635
and brisket for dinner tonight. Would you like to join us?

2150
01:23:49,635 --> 01:23:51,105
- Can I come over?
- Yes.

2151
01:23:51,105 --> 01:23:52,705
(I'd love to come.)

2152
01:23:52,705 --> 01:23:53,945
Are you out of your mind?

2153
01:23:53,945 --> 01:23:56,315
- You can't invite him over.
- Why not?

2154
01:23:56,715 --> 01:24:00,085
The lady with pink sunglasses. You don't like me, do you?

2155
01:24:00,485 --> 01:24:03,355
(The sassy Seoul girl with pink sunglasses)

2156
01:24:03,685 --> 01:24:04,785
Goodness.

2157
01:24:05,255 --> 01:24:06,925
Ladies, if you look over there and wave,

2158
01:24:06,925 --> 01:24:08,155
they'll take a photo of you.

2159
01:24:09,395 --> 01:24:11,225
If we look over there and wave, they'll take a photo of us.

2160
01:24:13,225 --> 01:24:14,865
(With the dashing captain)

2161
01:24:16,165 --> 01:24:18,635
Captain, it's sad to leave.

2162
01:24:18,635 --> 01:24:19,965
Come back again tomorrow.

2163
01:24:19,965 --> 01:24:23,405
(Saying goodbye to the captain with hopes to see him again)

2164
01:24:23,405 --> 01:24:25,045
- Let's go home.
- Let's go.

2165
01:24:25,145 --> 01:24:27,175
- You Seok, I'll drive.
- I had fun driving.

2166
01:24:28,275 --> 01:24:30,575
(Yoon Seo is driving instead of You Seok.)

2167
01:24:30,575 --> 01:24:32,745
- I'm having a lot of fun.
- Me too.

2168
01:24:32,745 --> 01:24:34,755
- Yes, it's great.
- Actually, I was a bit scared.

2169
01:24:34,855 --> 01:24:36,255
- About driving the boat?
- Everything.

2170
01:24:36,255 --> 01:24:38,485
- Everything we did today...
- I see.

2171
01:24:38,625 --> 01:24:40,255
- including harvesting sea squirts.
- Now that you've done it...

2172
01:24:40,255 --> 01:24:41,425
It's fun.

2173
01:24:41,895 --> 01:24:43,425
It was fun to clean sea squirts...

2174
01:24:43,425 --> 01:24:45,965
for the first time.

2175
01:24:46,095 --> 01:24:47,095
I see.

2176
01:24:47,865 --> 01:24:49,835
- Yoon Seo, are you having fun too?
- Yes, I'm having a lot of fun.

2177
01:24:49,835 --> 01:24:50,835
I see.

2178
01:24:51,065 --> 01:24:53,365
- It's so good to hear...
- That's cute.

2179
01:24:53,365 --> 01:24:55,075
- that you're having fun.
- I agree.

2180
01:24:55,135 --> 01:24:56,235
It's a lot of fun.

2181
01:24:56,235 --> 01:24:58,575
I get to try everything that I couldn't normally do.

2182
01:24:58,575 --> 01:25:01,315
- It's important that you have fun.
- They're very...

2183
01:25:01,415 --> 01:25:03,645
- positive, innocent, and kind.
- They have pure hearts.

2184
01:25:03,645 --> 01:25:05,915
I'm so happy to hear that you're enjoying yourselves.

2185
01:25:05,915 --> 01:25:07,615
- They're bright and genuine.
- Right.

2186
01:25:07,615 --> 01:25:09,155
(It was even more enjoyable as the four siblings were together.)

2187
01:25:09,315 --> 01:25:11,055
Once we arrive and cook fast,

2188
01:25:11,625 --> 01:25:13,585
we'll be done in an hour.

2189
01:25:13,585 --> 01:25:15,055
- We'll be able to eat in an hour.
- Yes.

2190
01:25:15,225 --> 01:25:16,755
I'm excited for dinner.

2191
01:25:17,555 --> 01:25:19,765
- I think I will really enjoy it.
- It will be good.

2192
01:25:21,865 --> 01:25:22,965
We're here.

2193
01:25:23,165 --> 01:25:24,665
- Thank you.
- Well done.

2194
01:25:24,665 --> 01:25:26,205
- Well done.
- Thank you for driving.

2195
01:25:26,435 --> 01:25:28,105
Doesn't it feel like we're back home?

2196
01:25:30,575 --> 01:25:32,045
(Soon, it's painted in warm shades of orange.)

2197
01:25:32,045 --> 01:25:36,475
(Sopo Village in Tongyeong)

2198
01:25:37,545 --> 01:25:41,485
(With the sunset comes dinnertime.)

2199
01:25:42,085 --> 01:25:45,955
(What kind of seasonal dishes are the neighbors preparing today?)

2200
01:25:47,425 --> 01:25:50,695
(Follow me, meow.)

2201
01:25:51,295 --> 01:25:54,165
(Sopo Village leader, Song Ok Ja's house)

2202
01:25:54,595 --> 01:25:56,435
I already seasoned it with salt.

2203
01:25:56,595 --> 01:25:58,165
Now, just slice it like this.

2204
01:26:00,065 --> 01:26:01,535
Add crushed garlic.

2205
01:26:01,805 --> 01:26:04,745
Chop some carrots into small pieces and add them.

2206
01:26:05,545 --> 01:26:06,845
Add some chili powder.

2207
01:26:06,845 --> 01:26:07,945
(Season it with chili powder and Cheongyang chili pepper)

2208
01:26:07,945 --> 01:26:11,485
There shouldn't be any excess water. That's the key.

2209
01:26:13,215 --> 01:26:16,715
(The neighbor's dish 1: Seasoned sea squirt salad)

2210
01:26:17,455 --> 01:26:19,185
(Another seasonal ingredient from Tongyeong)

2211
01:26:19,185 --> 01:26:21,695
(Wild rock seaweed)

2212
01:26:21,695 --> 01:26:23,055
In Tongyeong,

2213
01:26:23,055 --> 01:26:25,095
we mix seaweed with bean sprouts.

2214
01:26:26,665 --> 01:26:28,995
Ground sesame, sesame oil.

2215
01:26:28,995 --> 01:26:31,035
(Seasoned with ground sesame, sesame oil, and tuna fish sauce...)

2216
01:26:31,035 --> 01:26:32,765
This is how we usually eat it.

2217
01:26:32,765 --> 01:26:36,135
(It's mixed to create a nutty and mild flavor.)

2218
01:26:37,105 --> 01:26:38,345
(The neighbor's dish 2)

2219
01:26:38,345 --> 01:26:39,775
(Seasoned rock seaweed and bean sprouts)

2220
01:26:40,745 --> 01:26:42,115
(A seasonal table by Song Ok Ja...)

2221
01:26:42,115 --> 01:26:43,415
(that's filled with the fresh aroma of Tongyeong's sea)

2222
01:26:43,415 --> 01:26:44,785
(Seasoned sea squirt salad, seasoned rock seaweed and bean sprouts...)

2223
01:26:45,515 --> 01:26:49,585
(What will the siblings' seasonal table feature today?)

2224
01:26:50,655 --> 01:26:51,955
(Grown in the clean water of the southern coast)

2225
01:26:51,955 --> 01:26:53,755
(Dinner prepared with fresh sea squirts)

2226
01:26:53,755 --> 01:26:55,395
What's on today's menu?

2227
01:26:55,625 --> 01:26:58,325
- Sea squirt doenjang jjigae.
- Doenjang jjigae.

2228
01:26:58,325 --> 01:26:59,925
We'll make doenjang jjigae with sea squirt.

2229
01:26:59,925 --> 01:27:02,495
There's also brisket.

2230
01:27:02,495 --> 01:27:03,795
- We bought some brisket.
- We'll grill sea squirts...

2231
01:27:03,795 --> 01:27:06,205
in the oil left from cooking brisket.

2232
01:27:06,205 --> 01:27:07,265
Right.

2233
01:27:07,905 --> 01:27:10,675
(A special transformation of sea squirts, normally enjoyed raw)

2234
01:27:11,305 --> 01:27:13,705
(Shall we start preparing dinner?)

2235
01:27:13,975 --> 01:27:15,715
Jung Ah, show me how to prepare the radish.

2236
01:27:15,715 --> 01:27:17,245
We'll cut the radish outside,

2237
01:27:17,245 --> 01:27:18,885
- so take it outside.
- Okay.

2238
01:27:19,845 --> 01:27:22,555
(For dinner tonight and a side dish for tomorrow morning)

2239
01:27:22,555 --> 01:27:24,955
(Preparing radish and cabbage kimchi first)

2240
01:27:24,955 --> 01:27:25,985
Gosh, it's big.

2241
01:27:27,855 --> 01:27:29,455
- First...
- Show me once, and I'll do it.

2242
01:27:29,455 --> 01:27:30,495
First,

2243
01:27:30,795 --> 01:27:33,095
we're going to season it with salt.

2244
01:27:33,095 --> 01:27:34,225
Before seasoning it with salt,

2245
01:27:35,265 --> 01:27:38,105
cut it like this.

2246
01:27:38,105 --> 01:27:39,765
(For radish and cabbage kimchi, slice the radish diagonally.)

2247
01:27:39,765 --> 01:27:41,275
- Like that?
- It shouldn't be so thick.

2248
01:27:41,275 --> 01:27:43,605
We're going to eat it tomorrow.

2249
01:27:43,605 --> 01:27:44,775
This is too thin.

2250
01:27:45,375 --> 01:27:46,975
- You know what I mean?
- Yes.

2251
01:27:46,975 --> 01:27:48,145
(This is easy enough.)

2252
01:27:48,145 --> 01:27:49,375
- I can do it, Jung Ah.
- Yes.

2253
01:27:49,615 --> 01:27:52,515
Jung Ah, what other ingredients should we wash...

2254
01:27:52,515 --> 01:27:53,645
or prepare?

2255
01:27:54,145 --> 01:27:55,385
Spring onions?

2256
01:27:55,815 --> 01:27:57,785
We have to wash all the spring onions.

2257
01:27:59,125 --> 01:28:03,625
(Sun Young starts chopping with confidence.)

2258
01:28:05,295 --> 01:28:06,765
(Missing)

2259
01:28:09,065 --> 01:28:11,165
(Struggling)

2260
01:28:13,335 --> 01:28:17,405
(Just in 1 second, she gets stuck on slicing the radish.)

2261
01:28:18,205 --> 01:28:20,675
(Embarrassed)

2262
01:28:20,845 --> 01:28:22,515
- You Seok.
- Yes?

2263
01:28:22,945 --> 01:28:24,145
Can you come here for a second?

2264
01:28:24,345 --> 01:28:25,445
I'll be right there.

2265
01:28:26,545 --> 01:28:27,585
You Seok.

2266
01:28:27,585 --> 01:28:28,615
(Captain Yum appears instead of You Seok.)

2267
01:28:28,615 --> 01:28:30,355
- What do you need?
- It's okay, Jung Ah.

2268
01:28:31,355 --> 01:28:32,455
(Startled)

2269
01:28:32,455 --> 01:28:34,225
- What do you need?
- It's okay, Jung Ah.

2270
01:28:35,355 --> 01:28:36,555
It's okay, Jung Ah.

2271
01:28:36,995 --> 01:28:37,995
- What?
- It's nothing.

2272
01:28:37,995 --> 01:28:39,295
- Is it not working?
- I got it.

2273
01:28:39,665 --> 01:28:40,795
It's perfect.

2274
01:28:41,265 --> 01:28:42,295
- Watch out for your hands.
- Yes?

2275
01:28:42,295 --> 01:28:43,765
It's okay, You Seok.

2276
01:28:43,765 --> 01:28:44,765
- What?
- I figured it out.

2277
01:28:44,765 --> 01:28:45,835
Watch out for your hands.

2278
01:28:45,835 --> 01:28:47,135
I can do it well.

2279
01:28:47,135 --> 01:28:48,205
I figured it out.

2280
01:28:48,535 --> 01:28:50,275
As soon as I saw Jung Ah, I figured it out.

2281
01:28:50,875 --> 01:28:52,905
When I saw Jung Ah's face,

2282
01:28:52,905 --> 01:28:55,145
