2300
01:29:33,785 --> 01:29:36,715
I have to make it the way she likes. Like radish and cabbage kimchi.

2301
01:29:36,715 --> 01:29:38,225
(While shaping it the way Jung Ah likes,)

2302
01:29:38,225 --> 01:29:40,085
(she probably eats more than what she shapes.)

2303
01:29:40,355 --> 01:29:42,295
This is more like radish kimchi. This won't work.

2304
01:29:42,295 --> 01:29:43,725
(Will her radish be okay?)

2305
01:29:43,725 --> 01:29:45,825
You know the chungmu gimbap type, right? Like this.

2306
01:29:47,495 --> 01:29:48,535
I'm done.

2307
01:29:48,995 --> 01:29:50,065
But...

2308
01:29:50,935 --> 01:29:51,965
What's wrong, Jung Ah?

2309
01:29:53,905 --> 01:29:54,975
- Let me do it again.
- It's too big.

2310
01:29:54,975 --> 01:29:56,935
- It's too big? Okay.
- Goodness.

2311
01:29:57,205 --> 01:29:58,545
Wait, I'll do it again.

2312
01:29:58,645 --> 01:30:00,345
- Jung Ah, is it too big?
- It's big.

2313
01:30:00,345 --> 01:30:01,445
We're eating it tomorrow.

2314
01:30:01,445 --> 01:30:03,445
If it's this big, when will it ever be ready?

2315
01:30:03,445 --> 01:30:04,445
(A brutal scolding)

2316
01:30:05,415 --> 01:30:07,445
Wait, I'll make them smaller.

2317
01:30:07,445 --> 01:30:09,755
(Wait, I'll make them smaller.)

2318
01:30:11,355 --> 01:30:15,225
(An emergency reduction surgery)

2319
01:30:15,525 --> 01:30:17,255
- Isn't this okay?
- Yes.

2320
01:30:17,425 --> 01:30:18,625
- Isn't this okay?
- You're doing well.

2321
01:30:19,265 --> 01:30:20,265
Nice.

2322
01:30:20,795 --> 01:30:24,135
(Her radish for radish and cabbage kimchi is approved.)

2323
01:30:25,235 --> 01:30:26,235
(Let's season the radish with salt.)

2324
01:30:26,235 --> 01:30:28,405
We're going to use it in doenjang jjigae.

2325
01:30:28,635 --> 01:30:29,735
Okay.

2326
01:30:30,935 --> 01:30:33,975
(And...)

2327
01:30:33,975 --> 01:30:36,645
(she's adding starch syrup?)

2328
01:30:37,745 --> 01:30:39,445
Gosh, starch syrup and...

2329
01:30:39,445 --> 01:30:40,945
(Even vinegar?)

2330
01:30:41,355 --> 01:30:43,885
I add salty, sour, and sweet flavors.

2331
01:30:44,055 --> 01:30:45,285
- My goodness.
- After adding all these,

2332
01:30:45,625 --> 01:30:47,585
let it sit in salt for an hour.

2333
01:30:48,225 --> 01:30:50,955
My goodness. I had no idea that you add starch syrup.

2334
01:30:51,665 --> 01:30:52,965
That's really fascinating.

2335
01:30:53,295 --> 01:30:55,665
You don't add it when you make ordinary kimchi.

2336
01:30:55,665 --> 01:30:56,865
You don't add starch syrup?

2337
01:30:56,865 --> 01:30:58,665
You add starch syrup and vinegar to radish and cabbage kimchi?

2338
01:30:58,665 --> 01:31:00,805
We're going to use it to make chungmu gimbap.

2339
01:31:01,835 --> 01:31:03,835
We'll cover it...

2340
01:31:03,835 --> 01:31:05,145
- and let it sit for an hour.
- Okay.

2341
01:31:06,575 --> 01:31:09,215
(Captain Yum is making seasoning for radish and cabbage kimchi.)

2342
01:31:09,715 --> 01:31:10,775
Garlic.

2343
01:31:12,585 --> 01:31:13,645
Salted shrimp.

2344
01:31:14,015 --> 01:31:16,855
(Adding salted shrimp)

2345
01:31:17,555 --> 01:31:19,955
Add a tiny bit of anchovy sauce.

2346
01:31:20,055 --> 01:31:21,555
Green plum syrup.

2347
01:31:23,155 --> 01:31:24,425
(Chef Yum's Tip 1)

2348
01:31:24,425 --> 01:31:26,625
(Instead of glutinous rice paste, adding cooled rice)

2349
01:31:27,795 --> 01:31:30,035
(Chef Yum's Tip 2)

2350
01:31:30,035 --> 01:31:31,965
(Instead of a pear for the refreshing flavor,)

2351
01:31:31,965 --> 01:31:33,905
(you can use a pear drink.)

2352
01:31:34,235 --> 01:31:37,105
(Blend everything together until smooth.)

2353
01:31:37,105 --> 01:31:38,145
That's good.

2354
01:31:39,275 --> 01:31:41,745
(The seasoning is ready for making radish and cabbage kimchi.)

2355
01:31:43,015 --> 01:31:44,915
(Let's mix it with radish.)

2356
01:31:45,985 --> 01:31:49,255
(Coating the radish with chili powder)

2357
01:31:49,815 --> 01:31:52,485
(Why chili powder is added separately despite the seasoning)

2358
01:31:53,255 --> 01:31:55,295
(Chili powder helps the seasoning cling evenly...)

2359
01:31:55,295 --> 01:31:57,695
(to the radish and gives kimchi its signature spicy kick.)

2360
01:31:58,265 --> 01:32:00,395
(Adding spring onions)

2361
01:32:01,435 --> 01:32:04,035
(Adding the seasoning she made in advance)

2362
01:32:04,935 --> 01:32:07,365
(Mixing thoroughly)

2363
01:32:08,905 --> 01:32:13,305
(When Chef Yum's special touch is added)

2364
01:32:14,305 --> 01:32:17,075
(It looks so good that you want to eat it with some white rice.)

2365
01:32:18,315 --> 01:32:22,615
(A bite to see if it turned out well)

2366
01:32:22,755 --> 01:32:24,925
(Spicy and crunchy)

2367
01:32:25,885 --> 01:32:26,885
You Seok.

2368
01:32:26,885 --> 01:32:30,625
(Since it's tasty, the third eldest gets a bite.)

2369
01:32:32,365 --> 01:32:33,565
- It's good.
- Is it good?

2370
01:32:33,665 --> 01:32:34,835
(Gasping)

2371
01:32:34,835 --> 01:32:35,865
That's amazing.

2372
01:32:37,265 --> 01:32:38,505
- Yoon Seo.
- Yes?

2373
01:32:39,065 --> 01:32:43,005
(She also gives a bite to the youngest.)

2374
01:32:43,235 --> 01:32:44,975
Isn't it a little salty?

2375
01:32:44,975 --> 01:32:46,445
- It's so good.
- Is it?

2376
01:32:46,445 --> 01:32:48,645
- It's so good, Jung Ah.
- Is it? I'm glad.

2377
01:32:48,645 --> 01:32:50,475
I can't believe...

2378
01:32:50,675 --> 01:32:52,345
I get to taste your food.

2379
01:32:54,885 --> 01:32:56,485
I've really wanted to try it.

2380
01:32:57,055 --> 01:32:59,925
Yoon Seo, which container would you like the kimchi in?

2381
01:32:59,925 --> 01:33:01,225
I'll do it.

2382
01:33:01,655 --> 01:33:02,925
- Kimchi?
- Yes. Just give me the plate,

2383
01:33:02,925 --> 01:33:03,955
