2427
01:35:08,985 --> 01:35:12,985
(to show off my manly side?)

2428
01:35:13,455 --> 01:35:14,525
(Putting down)

2429
01:35:14,525 --> 01:35:15,755
(Putting down)

2430
01:35:16,025 --> 01:35:19,425
(I can handle holding the fire with my hands.)

2431
01:35:19,565 --> 01:35:21,325
I think the fire will get strong rather quickly.

2432
01:35:22,765 --> 01:35:24,835
(He pretentiously searches for the next target.)

2433
01:35:24,835 --> 01:35:26,005
This.

2434
01:35:26,505 --> 01:35:27,705
(Surprised)

2435
01:35:27,705 --> 01:35:29,135
(Taken back)

2436
01:35:29,205 --> 01:35:30,275
Gosh, this...

2437
01:35:30,875 --> 01:35:32,045
(Grunting)

2438
01:35:32,905 --> 01:35:34,405
(The cauldron is too heavy for him.)

2439
01:35:35,445 --> 01:35:36,645
It's so heavy.

2440
01:35:36,645 --> 01:35:37,675
(Waddling)

2441
01:35:38,885 --> 01:35:42,055
(He overcomes the weight and places it on the brazier.)

2442
01:35:43,155 --> 01:35:44,215
Actually,

2443
01:35:44,755 --> 01:35:47,925
it's my first time igniting a fire, and it's burning well.

2444
01:35:47,985 --> 01:35:50,025
It's easy to start a fire. It's not hard.

2445
01:35:50,025 --> 01:35:51,025
(Acting cocky)

2446
01:35:51,625 --> 01:35:54,995
(Let's start with thin-sliced pork belly.)

2447
01:35:55,665 --> 01:35:57,895
(He starts...)

2448
01:35:57,895 --> 01:36:00,735
